7e4","verification":{"payload":"tree bdf884435f84e2c440c9d315315487116f6065ae\nparent 8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789018946 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1789018946 -0700\n\nfix(title): the dev shell says Contact, like the tab does\n\n\"Contact UI\" is the repo''s name, not the app''s.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAikjd3fTaeTXFS5f+MZQnet94sNPPidUuvcu6M53F+BUTTa340+oaFDw2EoI4Yf9r\nqewqMhM4uq0eRYHer+Aws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T05:44:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/5383553c81a903cabab9b3c725d5adb9bcfb37e4","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDUzODM1NTNjODFhOTAzY2FiYWI5YjNjNzI1ZDVhZGI5YmNmYjM3ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c","sha":"8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c"}],"sha":"5383553c81a903cabab9b3c725d5adb9bcfb37e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/5383553c81a903cabab9b3c725d5adb9bcfb37e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T01:14:26Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T01:14:40Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(admin): give the operator a link that is not the guest''s invite\n\nThe command station rendered apt.meeting_link as ''Join Meeting''. On a Discord\nbooking that is a maxUses:1 invite minted for one specific guest, so the\noperator''s own admin UI was offering them the single link they must not use.\n\nAdds operator_link, DERIVED per row rather than stored: a Discord booking with\na real space gets a guild URL, which Discord opens in the viewer''s own session.\nNo column, no migration, and nothing that can fall out of sync with the space it\npoints at.\n\nNull for everything else, deliberately. A Jitsi room or a Meet link is already\nthe right link for everyone, and a pre-space Discord booking carries the SHARED\ninvite, which the operator can click without consuming anything — so the UI\nkeeps showing meeting_link in those cases rather than gaining a second link that\nadds nothing.\n\nplatform is NULLABLE on a stored appointment (migration 0009 made it optional\nfor admin-created events that name no platform), which the typecheck caught and\na hand-written signature would not have. Pinned by a test.\n\nThe guild URL is what was asked for and all contact-api can derive today: the\nspace''s chat channel id lives in ArchiveBot''s store and is not returned by\n/api/spaces/provision. Returning it there would make this a deep link into the\nspecific space, which is strictly better if the guild root proves annoying.","tree":{"sha":"48517b634cacb1317a9d480a50e50f87ef0496c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/48517b634cacb1317a9d480a50e50f87ef0496c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c","verification":{"payload":"tree 48517b634cacb1317a9d480a50e50f87ef0496c9\nparent 3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788830066 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788830080 -0700\n\nfeat(admin): give the operator a link that is not the guest''s invite\n\nThe command station rendered apt.meeting_link as ''Join Meeting''. On a Discord\nbooking that is a maxUses:1 invite minted for one specific guest, so the\noperator''s own admin UI was offering them the single link they must not use.\n\nAdds operator_link, DERIVED per row rather than stored: a Discord booking with\na real space gets a guild URL, which Discord opens in the viewer''s own session.\nNo column, no migration, and nothing that can fall out of sync with the space it\npoints at.\n\nNull for everything else, deliberately. A Jitsi room or a Meet link is already\nthe right link for everyone, and a pre-space Discord booking carries the SHARED\ninvite, which the operator can click without consuming anything — so the UI\nkeeps showing meeting_link in those cases rather than gaining a second link that\nadds nothing.\n\nplatform is NULLABLE on a stored appointment (migration 0009 made it optional\nfor admin-created events that name no platform), which the typecheck caught and\na hand-written signature would not have. Pinned by a test.\n\nThe guild URL is what was asked for and all contact-api can derive today: the\nspace''s chat channel id lives in ArchiveBot''s store and is not returned by\n/api/spaces/provision. Returning it there would make this a deep link into the\nspecific space, which is strictly better if the guild root proves annoying.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIUxDKVJqj+UA1MOmYYwpFzdRSka1WIxpy6pY6pUXhDW6VSxWNy4VUaeuRNy9cNrJg\nDq742gPJ3Yrxfe9jQboQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-08T01:14:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDhjYjQyMWZlMzUyYmU4MjA2MGRlNjUxNTNjZTQ2YzM3OWE1ZTE5M2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd","sha":"3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd"}],"sha":"8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8cb421fe352be82060de65153ce46c379a5e193c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:31:48Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:31:59Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(discord): give every booking its own private meeting space\n\nA Discord booking handed every guest the same static server invite. They landed\nin the main guild and saw whatever @everyone sees — which is a strange thing to\ndo to a stranger who filled in a contact form. Now contact-api asks ArchiveBot\nto carve out an isolated space: a category holding a chat channel and a Meeting\nRoom, visible only to a role minted for that one guest, reached by a single-use\ninvite that assigns the role on join, and deleted after 8 days with the guest\nkicked.\n\nA FAILED PROVISION DOES NOT FALL BACK TO THE SHARED INVITE. That is the point\nof the module and the one behaviour worth arguing about. ArchiveBot is a local\nPM2 service behind a Cloudflare tunnel, so an outage is ordinary — but handing\nout the general server invite when the private space could not be built would\nturn an outage into a privacy regression, silently doing the exact thing spaces\nexist to prevent. A failed provision stores no link. That path is already\nhonest: submit.ts logs meeting_link_failed and the confirmation email says the\nlink could not be generated and asks them to reply.\n\nNo schema change. The spaceId rides in meeting_id, which already exists for\nexternal meeting ids, and the cancel path revokes by it. isSpaceId guards that:\npre-space bookings carry `discord-<slotId>` there, and sending one to the\nrevoke route would 404 on every old cancel.\n\nIdempotency keys off the slot id, so a retried submit reuses its space instead\nof burning three more channels of a 500-channel guild budget.\n\nThe label sent to ArchiveBot is operator-facing only — ArchiveBot names the\nchannels and role with an opaque token, because role names are visible in\nmention autocomplete and would otherwise announce who booked to the whole guild.\n\nWidened mirrorInBackground from Promise<CalendarPushResult> to Promise<unknown>.\nIt only fires and forgets; the old type described its first caller rather than\nwhat it does, and the calendar mirror is no longer the only background job on\na cancel.\n\nAdded TextEncoder/TextDecoder/AbortSignal to the api eslint globals for the\nsame reason `crypto` was already there — Workers provides them, but\n@cloudflare/workers-types declares them in a way no-undef cannot see.","tree":{"sha":"a0b021f17b21382bb1b0996d4c2531ac88ab347b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/a0b021f17b21382bb1b0996d4c2531ac88ab347b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd","verification":{"payload":"tree a0b021f17b21382bb1b0996d4c2531ac88ab347b\nparent 8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788762708 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788762719 -0700\n\nfeat(discord): give every booking its own private meeting space\n\nA Discord booking handed every guest the same static server invite. They landed\nin the main guild and saw whatever @everyone sees — which is a strange thing to\ndo to a stranger who filled in a contact form. Now contact-api asks ArchiveBot\nto carve out an isolated space: a category holding a chat channel and a Meeting\nRoom, visible only to a role minted for that one guest, reached by a single-use\ninvite that assigns the role on join, and deleted after 8 days with the guest\nkicked.\n\nA FAILED PROVISION DOES NOT FALL BACK TO THE SHARED INVITE. That is the point\nof the module and the one behaviour worth arguing about. ArchiveBot is a local\nPM2 service behind a Cloudflare tunnel, so an outage is ordinary — but handing\nout the general server invite when the private space could not be built would\nturn an outage into a privacy regression, silently doing the exact thing spaces\nexist to prevent. A failed provision stores no link. That path is already\nhonest: submit.ts logs meeting_link_failed and the confirmation email says the\nlink could not be generated and asks them to reply.\n\nNo schema change. The spaceId rides in meeting_id, which already exists for\nexternal meeting ids, and the cancel path revokes by it. isSpaceId guards that:\npre-space bookings carry `discord-<slotId>` there, and sending one to the\nrevoke route would 404 on every old cancel.\n\nIdempotency keys off the slot id, so a retried submit reuses its space instead\nof burning three more channels of a 500-channel guild budget.\n\nThe label sent to ArchiveBot is operator-facing only — ArchiveBot names the\nchannels and role with an opaque token, because role names are visible in\nmention autocomplete and would otherwise announce who booked to the whole guild.\n\nWidened mirrorInBackground from Promise<CalendarPushResult> to Promise<unknown>.\nIt only fires and forgets; the old type described its first caller rather than\nwhat it does, and the calendar mirror is no longer the only background job on\na cancel.\n\nAdded TextEncoder/TextDecoder/AbortSignal to the api eslint globals for the\nsame reason `crypto` was already there — Workers provides them, but\n@cloudflare/workers-types declares them in a way no-undef cannot see.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQANKNa6DpOmd4MjiXHPxiXn4qBwK2L++1wC6/ApqOVtzZGrIXmMidO0d2fOaVXCAdK\nxcPqWFIUEzb0p+eIcpDAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T06:35:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDM3ODY2ODJlMDA1NzIzNDRjMjNmMzg4MDc2ODk0ZDE2ZDE1MzFlZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d","sha":"8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d"}],"sha":"3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3786682e00572344c23f388076894d16d1531efd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:21:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T06:22:02Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(devvault): read ARCHIVEBOT_SPACES_WEBHOOK_SECRET for the spaces caller\n\nArchiveBot''s webhook server gained /api/spaces/{provision,revoke,sweep} —\nprivate, disposable Discord meeting spaces — and contact-api is the first\ncaller. The routes authenticate with an HMAC over the raw body under their\nOWN secret, deliberately not the events one: provisioning private channels\nand kicking members is a separate capability from creating guild events.\n\nDeclared here so the caller can be developed and tested locally against the\nreal secret. The ACL grant for devvault/hadoku-contact-ui is already in\nplace. The DEPLOYED worker gets it by a different mechanism —\nWORKER_CONFIGS[''contact-api''] in hadoku_site''s update_cloudflare_secrets.py\n— which is deliberately not done yet: fetch_from_broker exits on any\nmanifest secret the vault 404s, so adding it there before the value exists\nwould break the whole contact-api push, RESEND_API_KEY and\nEDGE_AUTH_SECRET included.","tree":{"sha":"241fa3e31c17fbbcb0f14f6fc3038a8f249b4942","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/241fa3e31c17fbbcb0f14f6fc3038a8f249b4942"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d","verification":{"payload":"tree 241fa3e31c17fbbcb0f14f6fc3038a8f249b4942\nparent 7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788762102 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788762122 -0700\n\nchore(devvault): read ARCHIVEBOT_SPACES_WEBHOOK_SECRET for the spaces caller\n\nArchiveBot''s webhook server gained /api/spaces/{provision,revoke,sweep} —\nprivate, disposable Discord meeting spaces — and contact-api is the first\ncaller. The routes authenticate with an HMAC over the raw body under their\nOWN secret, deliberately not the events one: provisioning private channels\nand kicking members is a separate capability from creating guild events.\n\nDeclared here so the caller can be developed and tested locally against the\nreal secret. The ACL grant for devvault/hadoku-contact-ui is already in\nplace. The DEPLOYED worker gets it by a different mechanism —\nWORKER_CONFIGS[''contact-api''] in hadoku_site''s update_cloudflare_secrets.py\n— which is deliberately not done yet: fetch_from_broker exits on any\nmanifest secret the vault 404s, so adding it there before the value exists\nwould break the whole contact-api push, RESEND_API_KEY and\nEDGE_AUTH_SECRET included.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDQ/ot+ePK1mKzGBuYgNqEuXVdG6ai6l7+a9OIaq1YKqNB/Lh4mpRH8T3J69aFidY0\nyRE8bcBWmgjW7bxaZFEQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T06:22:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDhiZjU0YTQ0YzYwYjI4YzM5NDIzYWI3MGM1OTE5NmY1ZjM0MzVkN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61","sha":"7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61"}],"sha":"8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8bf54a44c60b28c39423ab70c59196f5f3435d7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:56Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T05:57:56Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(husky): the error message ran a command instead of naming the flag\n\nUnescaped backticks inside a DOUBLE-quoted string are command substitution, so\nthe hook''s own failure message ran `--no-verify` as a command:\n\n  sh: 1: --no-verify: not found\n  ❌ TypeScript errors — fix before committing (or  to bypass).\n\nTwo things wrong at once: a spurious \"not found\" on stderr, and the substitution\nexpanding to nothing — so the message lost the very flag it exists to tell you\nabout, exactly when someone is reading it because their commit just failed.\n\nSingle-quoted, which is what the string wanted all along; there is nothing in it\nto expand.\n\nSame bug hadoku-jobplatform fixed in 1f61c63. Its CI-skip half is already\npresent here, so this is the remaining half.\n\nhadoku_site''s hooks are NOT affected — they escape the backticks (\\`--no-verify\\`)\nand print them literally.","tree":{"sha":"18d5b4880c37be9e38eb7485fab7c6b997da2fb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/18d5b4880c37be9e38eb7485fab7c6b997da2fb3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61","verification":{"payload":"tree 18d5b4880c37be9e38eb7485fab7c6b997da2fb3\nparent a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788760676 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788760676 -0700\n\nfix(husky): the error message ran a command instead of naming the flag\n\nUnescaped backticks inside a DOUBLE-quoted string are command substitution, so\nthe hook''s own failure message ran `--no-verify` as a command:\n\n  sh: 1: --no-verify: not found\n  ❌ TypeScript errors — fix before committing (or  to bypass).\n\nTwo things wrong at once: a spurious \"not found\" on stderr, and the substitution\nexpanding to nothing — so the message lost the very flag it exists to tell you\nabout, exactly when someone is reading it because their commit just failed.\n\nSingle-quoted, which is what the string wanted all along; there is nothing in it\nto expand.\n\nSame bug hadoku-jobplatform fixed in 1f61c63. Its CI-skip half is already\npresent here, so this is the remaining half.\n\nhadoku_site''s hooks are NOT affected — they escape the backticks (\\`--no-verify\\`)\nand print them literally.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGchsiWFrSZoW9DiB2+D+ToztPSYRIWIvtfr2Ble7gBRpqvMnwr8PC179XAKxn/oya\noAYTJN/gLbRHASdDEswQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T05:58:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDdkYTJmY2U3YWY2NjU3OTI2NTVjNTM0NDNmMjRmYTRiODg3YmFlNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7","sha":"a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7"}],"sha":"7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/7da2fce7af665792655c53443f24fa4b887bae61"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:53:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T01:53:42Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(husky): skip the pre-commit hook in CI, where its gates cannot authenticate\n\nThe auto-update workflow''s \"Commit and push if changed\" step fires this hook.\nIts gates shell out to pnpm, and that step sets no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so\nsetup-node''s .npmrc resolves ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} to its own placeholder literal\nand the install answers 401 against a private @wolffm package.\n\nIt hides for months. The \"Update @wolffm/* to latest\" step above installs WITH\nthe token, leaving the store warm enough that the hook''s install never has to\nfetch. It breaks on the one package not in the store yet — a version published\nminutes earlier, which is precisely what this workflow exists to pick up.\nhadoku-jobplatform hit it on 2026-09-05 and failed its whole fan-out.\n\nNothing in the hook is load-bearing in CI, and that was checked here rather\nthan assumed: CI runs the lint, format and typecheck gates as their own jobs,\nand publish.yml walks from the registry''s latest to the first unpublished\nversion rather than trusting the committed one — its own comment says CI bumps\n\"are published but never committed back, so the committed version only falls\nbehind\". The hook''s version bump is therefore a convenience for local commits,\nnot a link in the publish chain.\n\nHUSKY=0 already existed as an escape but nothing set it; this keys on CI /\nGITHUB_ACTIONS, which the runner sets for us. Local commits are unaffected —\nverified both branches.","tree":{"sha":"51d9859ec2abc99076db7a3e94d0e55764363a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/51d9859ec2abc99076db7a3e94d0e55764363a49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 51d9859ec2abc99076db7a3e94d0e55764363a49\nparent a065e2efab06cb935ff7001589b9113cbcae190f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788746022 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788746022 -0700\n\nfix(husky): skip the pre-commit hook in CI, where its gates cannot authenticate\n\nThe auto-update workflow''s \"Commit and push if changed\" step fires this hook.\nIts gates shell out to pnpm, and that step sets no NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, so\nsetup-node''s .npmrc resolves ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} to its own placeholder literal\nand the install answers 401 against a private @wolffm package.\n\nIt hides for months. The \"Update @wolffm/* to latest\" step above installs WITH\nthe token, leaving the store warm enough that the hook''s install never has to\nfetch. It breaks on the one package not in the store yet — a version published\nminutes earlier, which is precisely what this workflow exists to pick up.\nhadoku-jobplatform hit it on 2026-09-05 and failed its whole fan-out.\n\nNothing in the hook is load-bearing in CI, and that was checked here rather\nthan assumed: CI runs the lint, format and typecheck gates as their own jobs,\nand publish.yml walks from the registry''s latest to the first unpublished\nversion rather than trusting the committed one — its own comment says CI bumps\n\"are published but never committed back, so the committed version only falls\nbehind\". The hook''s version bump is therefore a convenience for local commits,\nnot a link in the publish chain.\n\nHUSKY=0 already existed as an escape but nothing set it; this keys on CI /\nGITHUB_ACTIONS, which the runner sets for us. Local commits are unaffected —\nverified both branches.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKKgdP9NedZAK3aXxWaqt56hg4xyZIWHq0aqx6nSEhW91aVBZRODnQx7X5Br2Bh4Ub\nj4pDxSlcki7Fuw3+9NvgI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T01:53:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGE2YmM5NjRkMmZhNmYyZmVhMzEwYmViMjg4OTBiMDNhMDVhMmNjYjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a065e2efab06cb935ff7001589b9113cbcae190f","sha":"a065e2efab06cb935ff7001589b9113cbcae190f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a065e2efab06cb935ff7001589b9113cbcae190f"}],"sha":"a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6bc964d2fa6f2fea310beb28890b03a05a2ccb7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"