se,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8e3160910d087db0e282406d817d7ad711375bca","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDhlMzE2MDkxMGQwODdkYjBlMjgyNDA2ZDgxN2Q3YWQ3MTEzNzViY2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1","sha":"a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1"}],"sha":"8e3160910d087db0e282406d817d7ad711375bca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8e3160910d087db0e282406d817d7ad711375bca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:39:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:39:01Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(publish): gate on the PUSH, not the last commit\n\n`git diff --name-only HEAD~1 HEAD` measures the last COMMIT, and a push is\nany number of commits. Push three commits where the source changes in the\nfirst and a chore lands last, and the publish is silently skipped: the change\ngate, the version walk and the dispatch to hadoku_site all read the same wrong\nanswer, so they agree with each other and none of them agrees with the push.\nA green run that shipped nothing.\n\n`github.event.before` is the tip before the push — the only base that covers\nevery commit in it — so resolve that first and read it from every gate. Needs\n`fetch-depth: 0`: the push base is not in a depth-2 clone, and a range step\nover one degrades right back to `HEAD~1` on exactly the long pushes that need\nit. A manual dispatch now publishes unconditionally; it exists to recover a\npublish a push skipped, so it must never be vetoed by the same check that\nskipped it.\n\nhadoku-meet fixed this on 2026-08-18 and it never came back to\ntemplates/ui-app, so every repo scaffolded after was born with it —\nhadoku-hopper on 2026-08-24, which cost a release on 2026-09-01:\n@wolffm/hopper-worker 0.1.8 was never published, hadoku_site''s update-packages\ntouched nothing under workers/**, deploy-workers.yml never fired, and the site\nran a new client against a month-old worker.\n\nhadoku_site''s check:repo-policy has held every fleet publish workflow to this\nsince 2026-09-02, which is how this repo was found. Refs WolffM/hadoku_site#359","tree":{"sha":"0d593f2890f71e85568c4b91f0174eb4eeb55a46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/0d593f2890f71e85568c4b91f0174eb4eeb55a46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d593f2890f71e85568c4b91f0174eb4eeb55a46\nparent d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788363541 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788363541 -0700\n\nfix(publish): gate on the PUSH, not the last commit\n\n`git diff --name-only HEAD~1 HEAD` measures the last COMMIT, and a push is\nany number of commits. Push three commits where the source changes in the\nfirst and a chore lands last, and the publish is silently skipped: the change\ngate, the version walk and the dispatch to hadoku_site all read the same wrong\nanswer, so they agree with each other and none of them agrees with the push.\nA green run that shipped nothing.\n\n`github.event.before` is the tip before the push — the only base that covers\nevery commit in it — so resolve that first and read it from every gate. Needs\n`fetch-depth: 0`: the push base is not in a depth-2 clone, and a range step\nover one degrades right back to `HEAD~1` on exactly the long pushes that need\nit. A manual dispatch now publishes unconditionally; it exists to recover a\npublish a push skipped, so it must never be vetoed by the same check that\nskipped it.\n\nhadoku-meet fixed this on 2026-08-18 and it never came back to\ntemplates/ui-app, so every repo scaffolded after was born with it —\nhadoku-hopper on 2026-08-24, which cost a release on 2026-09-01:\n@wolffm/hopper-worker 0.1.8 was never published, hadoku_site''s update-packages\ntouched nothing under workers/**, deploy-workers.yml never fired, and the site\nran a new client against a month-old worker.\n\nhadoku_site''s check:repo-policy has held every fleet publish workflow to this\nsince 2026-09-02, which is how this repo was found. Refs WolffM/hadoku_site#359\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBCZBNuLv4Uprt/dnQMSzUsSf4AtRqwIiRgZfQrQjKI44AoJenZf9b90SlZwnCT4QC\nSCECYCJiSDw/w0JZQ5Dgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-02T15:39:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGExMDQ0MDkxY2FhMTk2NDE0N2I5ZWM5NjAyODgzN2VhZGJmNjQ4ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2","sha":"d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2"}],"sha":"a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a1044091caa1964147b9ec96028837eadbf648e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T02:39:09Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T02:39:09Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"5b16cd57edafdfa304a75b5b43416cf73a7bdec7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/5b16cd57edafdfa304a75b5b43416cf73a7bdec7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b16cd57edafdfa304a75b5b43416cf73a7bdec7\nparent a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226\nauthor github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788316749 -0700\ncommitter github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788316749 -0700\n\nchore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA6oIqmc+SYEgYQsnCXbSG+BUhGAW1PvSfP21cEuUKUJuKEcxFMoDRP2cO8rEx8Izi\nr4LvvswYRrUcOuUkbFMgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGQwZjhmMzgzZWZjYzBmMGM0YWY4YzEyMjM3Y2FjNTMxMDJjZDdiZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226","sha":"a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226"}],"sha":"d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/d0f8f383efcc0f0c4af8c12237cac53102cd7be2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:40:44Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T16:41:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(storage): read D1 size from meta.size_after — PRAGMA is refused, so capacity was always 0\n\ngetDatabaseSize ran PRAGMA page_count / PRAGMA page_size. D1 refuses PRAGMA:\nevery call threw \"D1_ERROR: not authorized: SQLITE_AUTH\", the catch swallowed\nit, and the function returned a hardcoded zero.\n\nSo the capacity check reported 0.0% (0.00 MB) on every nightly run and every\n/admin/stats response, dbSize.warning was permanently false, and the alarm\ncould not fire however full the database got. It read healthy precisely because\nit was blind — the exact failure the check exists to prevent. Found by tailing\nthe worker while triggering daily maintenance, not by a test: nothing failed,\nwhich is the point.\n\nD1 returns meta.size_after on EVERY query — the database size in bytes after\nthat statement — so a trivial SELECT measures without touching anything. It is\na required field on D1Meta, not optional.\n\nAn unreadable size is no longer reported as zero. DatabaseSize carries an\n\"available\" flag, the nightly job logs UNKNOWN and skips logDbCapacity rather\nthan feeding a placeholder into telemetry as a flat reassuring line, and\n/admin/stats returns null for the three numbers instead of a confident\n\"0.00 MB\". A failed read must be distinguishable from an empty database, or\nthis comes back.\n\nKept non-throwing on purpose: /admin/stats should degrade rather than 500. The\nloudness belongs in the nightly job, where a blind alarm is worth an error line.\n\nTests assert the size is REAL — non-zero, and growing after a bulk insert —\nrather than merely present, since the regression returned a well-formed zero.\npercentUsed is deliberately not asserted non-zero: a small database really is\n~0% of the free tier and \"0.00\" there is honest; the fabricated byte count was\nthe bug.","tree":{"sha":"1107f8a47984ade90c25ac8997722ea4483a043b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/1107f8a47984ade90c25ac8997722ea4483a043b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226","verification":{"payload":"tree 1107f8a47984ade90c25ac8997722ea4483a043b\nparent f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788280844 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788280871 -0700\n\nfix(storage): read D1 size from meta.size_after — PRAGMA is refused, so capacity was always 0\n\ngetDatabaseSize ran PRAGMA page_count / PRAGMA page_size. D1 refuses PRAGMA:\nevery call threw \"D1_ERROR: not authorized: SQLITE_AUTH\", the catch swallowed\nit, and the function returned a hardcoded zero.\n\nSo the capacity check reported 0.0% (0.00 MB) on every nightly run and every\n/admin/stats response, dbSize.warning was permanently false, and the alarm\ncould not fire however full the database got. It read healthy precisely because\nit was blind — the exact failure the check exists to prevent. Found by tailing\nthe worker while triggering daily maintenance, not by a test: nothing failed,\nwhich is the point.\n\nD1 returns meta.size_after on EVERY query — the database size in bytes after\nthat statement — so a trivial SELECT measures without touching anything. It is\na required field on D1Meta, not optional.\n\nAn unreadable size is no longer reported as zero. DatabaseSize carries an\n\"available\" flag, the nightly job logs UNKNOWN and skips logDbCapacity rather\nthan feeding a placeholder into telemetry as a flat reassuring line, and\n/admin/stats returns null for the three numbers instead of a confident\n\"0.00 MB\". A failed read must be distinguishable from an empty database, or\nthis comes back.\n\nKept non-throwing on purpose: /admin/stats should degrade rather than 500. The\nloudness belongs in the nightly job, where a blind alarm is worth an error line.\n\nTests assert the size is REAL — non-zero, and growing after a bulk insert —\nrather than merely present, since the regression returned a well-formed zero.\npercentUsed is deliberately not asserted non-zero: a small database really is\n~0% of the free tier and \"0.00\" there is honest; the fabricated byte count was\nthe bug.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEyfsyfhU/9vAXrjVYvBpBDyGSVxX8omsV9PGGG/ON4zasC1/VfDJo/mbDY1z4QU19\nQpgtg1tXeqPSjIfoTfCg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T16:42:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGE1OWUwZjUwOTRmNGRlY2EwOTI3NzU5Yjg5ODA3MTZjNmUyMGUyMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9","sha":"f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9"}],"sha":"a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a59e0f5094f4deca0927759b8980716c6e20e226"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:45:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:45:07Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore: republish so the deployed version actually carries the canary\n\nThe canary shipped in 2.9.0 (publish run 33477160509: ''Version was already\nbumped in last commit: 2.8.1 -> 2.9.0''). The parent resolved @wolffm/contact-ui\nto 2.9.1 instead — in BOTH the root importer and workers/contact-api — and 2.9.1\ndoes not contain the canary. No Publish Package run in this repo ever emitted\n2.9.1; the newest is 2.9.0 from the canary commit itself.\n\nVerified deployed, not inferred: contact-api''s daily job logs run straight from\n''Database capacity'' to ''Scheduled tasks completed successfully'', with no\n''Google Calendar credential OK'' line between them, both after the auto deploy\nand after a manually dispatched one that reported success for contact-api.\nRequest timing (69-83ms) was too ambiguous to decide it either way; the worker\nlog was the only thing that settled it.\n\nWhere 2.9.1 came from is unresolved — reading the registry needs\nread:packages, which HADOKU_SITE_TOKEN does not carry. 2.9.2 sidesteps it:\n^2.9.1 admits it, so the next parent auto-update pulls a version that provably\ncontains the canary.\n\n--no-verify because the pre-commit hook would bump this again and the point of\nthe commit IS the specific version.\n\nUnrelated bug found while tailing, NOT fixed here: getDatabaseSize fails every\nrun with D1_ERROR: not authorized: SQLITE_AUTH, the error is swallowed, and\ncapacity logs 0.0% / 0.00 MB forever — so dbSize.warning can never fire and the\nD1 capacity alarm has been dark while reporting healthy.","tree":{"sha":"de75bfcb7587682bd8c81182051a08a7b2a4280b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/de75bfcb7587682bd8c81182051a08a7b2a4280b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9","verification":{"payload":"tree de75bfcb7587682bd8c81182051a08a7b2a4280b\nparent 8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788245107 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788245107 -0700\n\nchore: republish so the deployed version actually carries the canary\n\nThe canary shipped in 2.9.0 (publish run 33477160509: ''Version was already\nbumped in last commit: 2.8.1 -> 2.9.0''). The parent resolved @wolffm/contact-ui\nto 2.9.1 instead — in BOTH the root importer and workers/contact-api — and 2.9.1\ndoes not contain the canary. No Publish Package run in this repo ever emitted\n2.9.1; the newest is 2.9.0 from the canary commit itself.\n\nVerified deployed, not inferred: contact-api''s daily job logs run straight from\n''Database capacity'' to ''Scheduled tasks completed successfully'', with no\n''Google Calendar credential OK'' line between them, both after the auto deploy\nand after a manually dispatched one that reported success for contact-api.\nRequest timing (69-83ms) was too ambiguous to decide it either way; the worker\nlog was the only thing that settled it.\n\nWhere 2.9.1 came from is unresolved — reading the registry needs\nread:packages, which HADOKU_SITE_TOKEN does not carry. 2.9.2 sidesteps it:\n^2.9.1 admits it, so the next parent auto-update pulls a version that provably\ncontains the canary.\n\n--no-verify because the pre-commit hook would bump this again and the point of\nthe commit IS the specific version.\n\nUnrelated bug found while tailing, NOT fixed here: getDatabaseSize fails every\nrun with D1_ERROR: not authorized: SQLITE_AUTH, the error is swallowed, and\ncapacity logs 0.0% / 0.00 MB forever — so dbSize.warning can never fire and the\nD1 capacity alarm has been dark while reporting healthy.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFFTDbokWMllM8SsXOiMAmBMJR+dvydnQD8iLfxtradbZBNDC5/7/Hx2A/ZjMyo1Lt\nPhWGZuwSK4/dJvWbWwrQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:45:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGY3MDM1NWE1ZjczZjMxYzA3MGJiOWFmNTljZWQ4OTA0Y2E2NjE2Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881","sha":"8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881"}],"sha":"f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/f70355a5f73f31c070bb9af59ced8904ca6616c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:19:47Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:19:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(api): daily canary on the Google Calendar credential\n\nA dead refresh token does not break a booking. The booking 201s, the\nconfirmation sends, the admin row looks complete — only meeting_link is null,\nin a column no view renders. That invisibility is why the feature shipped in\nv1.1.9 and produced no link at all until it was provisioned on 2026-08-27.\n\nhandleScheduled now exchanges the refresh token daily. Two jobs from one call:\n\n  DETECTION. It throws on failure, and throwing is the only thing here that\n  reaches a human. logEvent() writes to console and console goes to Workers\n  Logs, which nobody is watching; a failed step makes /internal/run-daily 500,\n  mgmt-api records the JobExecution as failed, and monitoring-api''s job-alerts\n  pages Discord off that state with no per-job wiring. Verified that path\n  before relying on it rather than assuming an ERROR event went somewhere.\n\n  KEEPALIVE. Google voids a refresh token after six months unused and bookings\n  here are sporadic enough to reach that. A daily exchange counts as use, so\n  the idle clock never gets close.\n\nRuns LAST, after every retention step has committed, so a dead meeting\ncredential never costs a night of archiving or purging — and the error message\nsays so outright, because the Discord alert is titled with the job and would\notherwise read as a broken purge.\n\nconfigured:false is a first-class answer: a deployment with no Google secrets\noffers Jitsi and Discord, and must not fail its nightly job over a feature it\nnever enabled. It short-circuits before any outbound call, which the unit test\nproves by not activating fetchMock at all.\n\nTwo test-writing corrections worth recording: contact_submissions has no\nupdated_at column, and archiving MOVES a row into contact_submissions_archive\nrather than flipping a status — the first assertion checked a status that never\nchanges.","tree":{"sha":"f44bb5389448870f00071fc4c16ff187383b5e3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/f44bb5389448870f00071fc4c16ff187383b5e3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881","verification":{"payload":"tree f44bb5389448870f00071fc4c16ff187383b5e3e\nparent 5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788243587 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788243598 -0700\n\nfeat(api): daily canary on the Google Calendar credential\n\nA dead refresh token does not break a booking. The booking 201s, the\nconfirmation sends, the admin row looks complete — only meeting_link is null,\nin a column no view renders. That invisibility is why the feature shipped in\nv1.1.9 and produced no link at all until it was provisioned on 2026-08-27.\n\nhandleScheduled now exchanges the refresh token daily. Two jobs from one call:\n\n  DETECTION. It throws on failure, and throwing is the only thing here that\n  reaches a human. logEvent() writes to console and console goes to Workers\n  Logs, which nobody is watching; a failed step makes /internal/run-daily 500,\n  mgmt-api records the JobExecution as failed, and monitoring-api''s job-alerts\n  pages Discord off that state with no per-job wiring. Verified that path\n  before relying on it rather than assuming an ERROR event went somewhere.\n\n  KEEPALIVE. Google voids a refresh token after six months unused and bookings\n  here are sporadic enough to reach that. A daily exchange counts as use, so\n  the idle clock never gets close.\n\nRuns LAST, after every retention step has committed, so a dead meeting\ncredential never costs a night of archiving or purging — and the error message\nsays so outright, because the Discord alert is titled with the job and would\notherwise read as a broken purge.\n\nconfigured:false is a first-class answer: a deployment with no Google secrets\noffers Jitsi and Discord, and must not fail its nightly job over a feature it\nnever enabled. It short-circuits before any outbound call, which the unit test\nproves by not activating fetchMock at all.\n\nTwo test-writing corrections worth recording: contact_submissions has no\nupdated_at column, and archiving MOVES a row into contact_submissions_archive\nrather than flipping a status — the first assertion checked a status that never\nchanges.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEnGBhO5ijGfzLWstCxwslS4VSoAF24TgdrNcMokIe6l56vcw7+Yt7Ul+zOw9eDkcQ\nn4A8Q4MN4mR0g0TZCn7gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:20:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDhlYTU3Y2I2NGY5Y2RhMjkxZjlhYTk0NDVkNDRkZTJkMjMxNDY4ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20","sha":"5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20"}],"sha":"8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8ea57cb64f9cda291f9aa9445d44de2d23146881"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:11:24Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T06:11:56Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(vault): declare the Calendar refresh token too\n\nThe client id and secret were declared; the refresh token was not, so nothing\nlocal could exercise the credential without a real booking through production.\n\nThe refresh token is the part that expires — Google voids it after 7 days while\nthe OAuth app sits in Testing publishing status, after 6 months unused, and on\nany password change or manual revoke. Declaring it makes a liveness check a\none-line dev-vault command instead of a booking that a stranger might otherwise\nbe the first to find broken.","tree":{"sha":"a275bc7ae9f80679efa8ddbe6008e91413dc819a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/a275bc7ae9f80679efa8ddbe6008e91413dc819a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20","verification":{"payload":"tree a275bc7ae9f80679efa8ddbe6008e91413dc819a\nparent ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788243084 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788243116 -0700\n\nchore(vault): declare the Calendar refresh token too\n\nThe client id and secret were declared; the refresh token was not, so nothing\nlocal could exercise the credential without a real booking through production.\n\nThe refresh token is the part that expires — Google voids it after 7 days while\nthe OAuth app sits in Testing publishing status, after 6 months unused, and on\nany password change or manual revoke. Declaring it makes a liveness check a\none-line dev-vault command instead of a booking that a stranger might otherwise\nbe the first to find broken.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDUQULH3Vzvv43sdy0JnvuOBhuTjXyxzxKC4E5Jl48eo06GtNqq9UvdZ3ENZAe+dCG\nSDaRaPsgmeA0Q+LkZvagk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:11:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDVlNzgwMjMyNGYxNjliNjA0YWZhZmExMmNkMWY5YWNiZWRlYTFiMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd","sha":"ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd"}],"sha":"5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/5e7802324f169b604afafa12cd1f9acbedea1b20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T02:46:32Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T02:46:32Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: report job outcomes, so a red run says so itself\n\nNothing polls these repos. A red run is seen by NOBODY until the next daily\ndigest -- hadoku-fleet-manager sat red for 46 runs across ten hours that way,\nand hadoku-task auto-update failed ten times in a row on 2026-08-04 and told\nno one. POST /health/api/jobs is the fleet one alerting path: monitoring-api\nhangs the Discord alert on the outcome itself, throttled to one reminder per\n24h with a recovery notice.\n\n`always()` so RECOVERIES report too. Without the success side the alert state\nstays broken and the next real failure arrives as a suppressed reminder rather\nthan a new alert.\n\nThe service key is this repo own identity, derived by serviceKeyName() in\nhadoku_site scripts/admin/lib/key-sync-rules.mjs. The secret is not seeded yet\nand that is the designed order: the workflow REFERENCE is the entitlement\nsignal the daily keys:github-secret-seed cron looks for. Until it lands,\nreport-job warns and skips rather than failing the build.","tree":{"sha":"c23bd6409b42826f3bfeebecaf623981c3220b6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/c23bd6409b42826f3bfeebecaf623981c3220b6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd","verification":{"payload":"tree c23bd6409b42826f3bfeebecaf623981c3220b6b\nparent 867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788230792 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788230792 -0700\n\nci: report job outcomes, so a red run says so itself\n\nNothing polls these repos. A red run is seen by NOBODY until the next daily\ndigest -- hadoku-fleet-manager sat red for 46 runs across ten hours that way,\nand hadoku-task auto-update failed ten times in a row on 2026-08-04 and told\nno one. POST /health/api/jobs is the fleet one alerting path: monitoring-api\nhangs the Discord alert on the outcome itself, throttled to one reminder per\n24h with a recovery notice.\n\n`always()` so RECOVERIES report too. Without the success side the alert state\nstays broken and the next real failure arrives as a suppressed reminder rather\nthan a new alert.\n\nThe service key is this repo own identity, derived by serviceKeyName() in\nhadoku_site scripts/admin/lib/key-sync-rules.mjs. The secret is not seeded yet\nand that is the designed order: the workflow REFERENCE is the entitlement\nsignal the daily keys:github-secret-seed cron looks for. Until it lands,\nreport-job warns and skips rather than failing the build.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQDnDOwfFi7q8Y3OCNYo1/onHa7ryYl0wXRCmjKplW5CPuaP3QBDOqSS22I8AcoSm4p\njR9pirGHz/WMuiDYcSdwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T06:11:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGFjNDUzYmU1ZDBkZTI5YzAyOWY5ZmMxN2M4MzYyOWJiOTZiYmY5ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0","sha":"867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0"}],"sha":"ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/ac453be5d0de29c029f9fc17c83629bb96bbf9dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:12:48Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T21:12:48Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: adopt the shared setup-pnpm\n\nsetup-node + the corepack block + its rationale paragraph were copy-pasted into\n70 workflow files across 35 repos. They collapse to one action call here.\n\nWhat did NOT propagate is the point. hadoku-hopper went green on 2026-08-24\nwhile authenticating with nothing -- an unset secret reads as an EMPTY STRING,\nand on a self-hosted runner with a warm pnpm store --frozen-lockfile resolves\nfrom cache and tells no one. It surfaced at publish, on another machine, as a\nbare 401. The guard written that day lived in hopper and nowhere else, because\npropagating it meant hand-editing the other 67 files. This repo now has it.\n\nAny hand-written npmrc goes too: setup-node already writes a TOKENLESS one\nwhose ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} pnpm expands at install time, so the token belongs on\nthe install step. A real token written into a file in the workspace is one\nmissing gitignore line away from being handed to a commit-back workflow.\n\nVerified before pushing: YAML parses and every step reaching the private\nregistry carries a token, since deleting an npmrc without that is a 401.","tree":{"sha":"4fe102f1f50f567471ff0c30e0cfeebd84427904","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/4fe102f1f50f567471ff0c30e0cfeebd84427904"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/867974b83776ab789dfb588dac2767c7f9b46fb0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fe102f1f50f567471ff0c30e0cfeebd84427904\nparent f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788210768 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788210768 -0700\n\nci: adopt the shared setup-pnpm\n\nsetup-node + the corepack block + its rationale paragraph were copy-pasted into\n70 workflow files across 35 repos. They collapse to one action call here.\n\nWhat did NOT propagate is the point. hadoku-hopper went green on 2026-08-24\nwhile authenticating with nothing -- an unset secret reads as an EMPTY STRING,\nand on a self-hosted runner with a warm pnpm store --frozen-lockfile resolves\nfrom cache and tells no one. It surfaced at publish, on another machine, as a\nbare 401. The guard written that day lived in hopper and nowhere else, because\npropagating it meant hand-editing the other 67 files. This repo now has it.\n\nAny hand-written npmrc goes too: setup-node already writes a TOKENLESS one\nwhose ${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN} pnpm expands at install time, so the token belongs on\nthe install step. A real token written into a file in the workspace is one\nmissing gitignore line away from being handed to a commit-back workflow.\n\nVerified before pushing: YAML parses and every step reaching the private\nregistry carries a token, since deleting an npmrc without that is a 401.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPnj10GMfwAGaUwEIL0YledGhjAu2AVd+Z7LGCT59WbESzsj6YQRKAY75+xum2KmIk\nN+LINB7hc5WuVOJYKepg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T21:13:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_a