https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:03:13Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T13:03:13Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"33b0b8dfbe0e223edc1fc9e80db8d5e59135b966","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/33b0b8dfbe0e223edc1fc9e80db8d5e59135b966"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 33b0b8dfbe0e223edc1fc9e80db8d5e59135b966\nparent 66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91\nauthor github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788181393 -0700\ncommitter github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788181393 -0700\n\nchore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAsNwtxoP2ycF1wnDLZycaYHPCFZKkwL3O+V4RoHBcmUspIMGVMebi2KrFC4eA79Yr\nymyEUM7Lub/yCoSxt65Qc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGY3MGQ4MWU3ZmQ0NDBmZTMzZjg1ZjhmNzkyYzE0NGMxNTkxM2M5ZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91","sha":"66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91"}],"sha":"f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/f70d81e7fd440fe33f85f8f792c144c15913c9d4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T00:31:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T00:31:34Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(api): move the service-tier route to its own prefix, and document tiering in one place\n\nv2.7.0 lowered the worker gate for PATCH /appointments/:id/status and could\nnever work: edge-router gates /contact/api/admin at admin tier and is crossed\nFIRST, so the request 403''d at the edge and never reached the worker. The 403\nbody gives it away — {\"error\":\"forbidden\",\"required\":\"admin\"} is\nedge-router''s shape, not this worker''s.\n\nedge-router matches exact-or-prefix only, so a service-tier route under /admin\nis unreachable unless the edge rule for the whole admin prefix is lowered —\nwhich would put appointment PII (names, emails, message bodies) behind service\ntier at the edge, leaving only the worker holding the line. So the route moves\nto its own prefix instead: /contact/api/service. /admin goes back to uniformly\nadmin with no carve-outs.\n\nOne handler, two mounts, two tiers: the command-station UI keeps calling\n/admin/appointments/:id/status at admin tier, automations use /service at\nservice tier, and neither can drift in behaviour from the other. A test pins\nthat the /admin mount does NOT inherit the lower gate.\n\nDocumentation is consolidated rather than added to. The rationale was\npreviously duplicated across three files, which is how comments start\ndisagreeing; it now lives once in CLAUDE.md under \"Admin and service\nsurfaces\" — the prefix table, the admission rule (a service route may ACT, it\nmay not DISCLOSE), the two-gate model, and how to tell which gate denied you.\nThe code comments were cut down to pointers.\n\nRequires the matching edge-router rule in hadoku_site to be deployed before\n/service is reachable at all.","tree":{"sha":"6e46e33a00efb0ae5a34428c43fc5ac7e8578f4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/6e46e33a00efb0ae5a34428c43fc5ac7e8578f4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91","verification":{"payload":"tree 6e46e33a00efb0ae5a34428c43fc5ac7e8578f4f\nparent 3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788136282 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788136294 -0700\n\nfeat(api): move the service-tier route to its own prefix, and document tiering in one place\n\nv2.7.0 lowered the worker gate for PATCH /appointments/:id/status and could\nnever work: edge-router gates /contact/api/admin at admin tier and is crossed\nFIRST, so the request 403''d at the edge and never reached the worker. The 403\nbody gives it away — {\"error\":\"forbidden\",\"required\":\"admin\"} is\nedge-router''s shape, not this worker''s.\n\nedge-router matches exact-or-prefix only, so a service-tier route under /admin\nis unreachable unless the edge rule for the whole admin prefix is lowered —\nwhich would put appointment PII (names, emails, message bodies) behind service\ntier at the edge, leaving only the worker holding the line. So the route moves\nto its own prefix instead: /contact/api/service. /admin goes back to uniformly\nadmin with no carve-outs.\n\nOne handler, two mounts, two tiers: the command-station UI keeps calling\n/admin/appointments/:id/status at admin tier, automations use /service at\nservice tier, and neither can drift in behaviour from the other. A test pins\nthat the /admin mount does NOT inherit the lower gate.\n\nDocumentation is consolidated rather than added to. The rationale was\npreviously duplicated across three files, which is how comments start\ndisagreeing; it now lives once in CLAUDE.md under \"Admin and service\nsurfaces\" — the prefix table, the admission rule (a service route may ACT, it\nmay not DISCLOSE), the two-gate model, and how to tell which gate denied you.\nThe code comments were cut down to pointers.\n\nRequires the matching edge-router rule in hadoku_site to be deployed before\n/service is reachable at all.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCtrY8xaWZvbvoFWcHOesh89sLRybM3RXJIBTU71Ty9RtSQKL6g9VH6NYjMsT34jNd\nu745NhZiip8jL0cMK0VAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T00:33:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDY2YmEzNjAxY2Q3OTg2MzhlZDg0YzFjYWQxMTkyOTdhZWQ1ZjNiOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368","sha":"3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368"}],"sha":"66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/66ba3601cd798638ed84c1cad119297aed5f3b91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T19:44:19Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T19:44:19Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore: stop tracking .claude/settings.local.json\n\nIt is a per-machine agent permission file — local by name and by nature. 44 of\nthe 50 checkouts on this host already ignore it; this was one of six that did\nnot, so every nightly repos:main-sync reported the repo as having uncommitted\nchanges and could never reach empty.\n\nA report that is permanently non-empty is a report nobody reads.","tree":{"sha":"81ded43352f02248c7a9bb3a16a00664b0e82e3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/81ded43352f02248c7a9bb3a16a00664b0e82e3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368","verification":{"payload":"tree 81ded43352f02248c7a9bb3a16a00664b0e82e3b\nparent 19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788119059 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788119059 -0700\n\nchore: stop tracking .claude/settings.local.json\n\nIt is a per-machine agent permission file — local by name and by nature. 44 of\nthe 50 checkouts on this host already ignore it; this was one of six that did\nnot, so every nightly repos:main-sync reported the repo as having uncommitted\nchanges and could never reach empty.\n\nA report that is permanently non-empty is a report nobody reads.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEh0fGV1kv/kMuFL6fT3dKwFK2HYYcWAnwmHn3paUKs7z1TDWI12m9qCz6V15l3uW+\n78BmmBlabnK4B2yVyBUgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T19:44:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDNjOTM0ZTczODcxNDM4NDg3ZTljNDAxNmZjMzI2MmNmNGIxMWYzNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f","sha":"19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f"}],"sha":"3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3c934e73871438487e9c4016fc3262cf4b11f368"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:28:15Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T05:28:15Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"refactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.","tree":{"sha":"89989c056f60814a79d290724bd4974ea2acdcf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/89989c056f60814a79d290724bd4974ea2acdcf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f","verification":{"payload":"tree 89989c056f60814a79d290724bd4974ea2acdcf8\nparent 8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067695 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1788067695 -0700\n\nrefactor(ci): the fleet manager owns node selection\n\n    - ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER || ''[\"self-hosted\",\"hadoku-builder\"]'') }}\n    + ${{ fromJSON(vars.CI_RUNNER) }}\n\nThat fallback was fleet internals pasted into every workflow: the label the\ntier monitor owns, the variable''s name, and the semantics of unset. Fleet-wide\nit was 107 workflows across 27 repos, so @wolffm/fleet-manager could not change\nhow it is addressed without editing the whole ecosystem.\n\nSafe because CI_RUNNER is already set here. fleet-manager 0.5.0 writes the\nfleet target to every covered repo instead of deleting the variable, and it is\nPERSISTENT repo state — if the fleet manager stops, the last value stays and CI\nkeeps scheduling.\n\nWhere a job carries the fork-PR author_association guard, only the trailing\nfleet fallback is removed; the guard that sends untrusted PRs to hosted runners\nis untouched.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJ8HKMik44/pqAgxU60Zc3D7YEENpAWNI0vMuo1BwAgQAW7LglLjFvspKBt4kgv/Zd\nxZOsavaUFwrqHkZhTkWQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T05:28:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDE5YjdjMTU2MmI2MGM2MGVlZjgwZTU5Yjk3MmE4ZDBmYzY0YTA0M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b","sha":"8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b"}],"sha":"19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/19b7c1562b60c60eef80e59b972a8d0fc64a043f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:29:25Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:29:37Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(admin): make appointment status changes service-tier, and only that\n\nCancelling a booking is an operational act an automation should be able to\nperform — retiring a test row, closing out a no-show — and it discloses\nnothing: PATCH /appointments/:id/status takes an id and a status and answers\nwith a boolean.\n\nThe rest of /admin is not that. createSubmissionRoutes serves every message the\ncontact form has ever received, with names, addresses, IPs and user agents;\ncreateEmailRoutes sends mail AS the operator; blocklist and templates are\noperator state. Service tier is held by every worker key in the ecosystem, so\nlowering the shared gate would have put the operator''s inbox behind any one of\nthem, or behind a bug in any one of them. It stays at admin.\n\nImplemented as two sub-apps over DISJOINT paths rather than a path-exception\ninside one middleware. An exception works on the day it is written and rots the\nmoment someone adds a route matching it; two gates over two route sets cannot\ndevelop that overlap without the same path being written into both files.\n\nThe service gate is bound to the exact path, not ''*''. Mounted at ''*'' it runs\nahead of the admin gate on every /admin request — still denied, since the admin\ngate is behind it, but denied with the wrong reason: an anonymous caller asking\nfor /submissions was told ''Service access required''. send-email.test.ts caught\nthat.\n\nadmin-tier-split.test.ts pins both halves: service can cancel, friend cannot\n(service is rank 2, friend 1 — lowering must not open), and a service key gets\n403 on all eight of the disclosing endpoints.","tree":{"sha":"13ff054713c3be9a2db4e885e12db0e674c86053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/13ff054713c3be9a2db4e885e12db0e674c86053"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b","verification":{"payload":"tree 13ff054713c3be9a2db4e885e12db0e674c86053\nparent 1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787876965 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787876977 -0700\n\nfeat(admin): make appointment status changes service-tier, and only that\n\nCancelling a booking is an operational act an automation should be able to\nperform — retiring a test row, closing out a no-show — and it discloses\nnothing: PATCH /appointments/:id/status takes an id and a status and answers\nwith a boolean.\n\nThe rest of /admin is not that. createSubmissionRoutes serves every message the\ncontact form has ever received, with names, addresses, IPs and user agents;\ncreateEmailRoutes sends mail AS the operator; blocklist and templates are\noperator state. Service tier is held by every worker key in the ecosystem, so\nlowering the shared gate would have put the operator''s inbox behind any one of\nthem, or behind a bug in any one of them. It stays at admin.\n\nImplemented as two sub-apps over DISJOINT paths rather than a path-exception\ninside one middleware. An exception works on the day it is written and rots the\nmoment someone adds a route matching it; two gates over two route sets cannot\ndevelop that overlap without the same path being written into both files.\n\nThe service gate is bound to the exact path, not ''*''. Mounted at ''*'' it runs\nahead of the admin gate on every /admin request — still denied, since the admin\ngate is behind it, but denied with the wrong reason: an anonymous caller asking\nfor /submissions was told ''Service access required''. send-email.test.ts caught\nthat.\n\nadmin-tier-split.test.ts pins both halves: service can cancel, friend cannot\n(service is rank 2, friend 1 — lowering must not open), and a service key gets\n403 on all eight of the disclosing endpoints.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFQyKCRlEQNryO5jt3XtJkX3AKnWAseLuOuM2LyWUPhRReGcVsmaXORIEFHYY1nhg3\nJP2OVI55AigPRhgl1NvgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T00:29:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDhiNjU1N2VkZGVlYTQ0ZGFlYjAyZDk0MjkyOWQyM2E5ZGQ5ZDljOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb","sha":"1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb"}],"sha":"8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8b6557eddeea44daeb02d942929d23a9dd9d9c9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T22:54:25Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T22:54:25Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(vault): declare the Google Calendar OAuth client credentials\n\nscripts/google-oauth-setup.mjs reads GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and\nGOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET from the environment. Declaring them here is what\nlets dev-vault inject them, so minting — and later re-minting, which is the\ndocumented recovery when Google expires the refresh token — is a vault-backed\ncommand instead of pasting secrets onto a command line.\n\nVault item names are the ones the operator created\n(HADOKU_MEETING_ORCHESTRATOR_GCP_*), not the MEETING_GOOGLE_* the provisioning\ndoc proposed; the doc gets corrected to match rather than the vault renamed.\n\nDeclaration only, no values, and no grant: the ACL is per-key and this file is\njust what key-acl-sync reads to decide what to grant.","tree":{"sha":"3dcbad9c7a778c4b025d2d80a09c410da41c1f88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/3dcbad9c7a778c4b025d2d80a09c410da41c1f88"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3dcbad9c7a778c4b025d2d80a09c410da41c1f88\nparent c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787871265 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787871265 -0700\n\nchore(vault): declare the Google Calendar OAuth client credentials\n\nscripts/google-oauth-setup.mjs reads GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID and\nGOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET from the environment. Declaring them here is what\nlets dev-vault inject them, so minting — and later re-minting, which is the\ndocumented recovery when Google expires the refresh token — is a vault-backed\ncommand instead of pasting secrets onto a command line.\n\nVault item names are the ones the operator created\n(HADOKU_MEETING_ORCHESTRATOR_GCP_*), not the MEETING_GOOGLE_* the provisioning\ndoc proposed; the doc gets corrected to match rather than the vault renamed.\n\nDeclaration only, no values, and no grant: the ACL is per-key and this file is\njust what key-acl-sync reads to decide what to grant.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFTyBJQgtCIoDXstPU6fgTt823f5Up+7lI1QvcIRDG3CF3J5RntrCjbyCJY+Npe8Hg\nHg8baEDGlte7dpaEgg6Qk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T22:54:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDFmYWYwMzg1NTJjMjkzOGMzMDRkMjAwYTU3Yjk4M2U5ZTQwM2E3ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09","sha":"c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09"}],"sha":"1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/1faf038552c2938c304d200a57b983e9e403a7fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:16:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T21:16:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(meetings): report a failed meeting link instead of promising one nothing sends\n\nA booking whose link generation failed was indistinguishable from one that\nworked. The route stored `undefined` and moved on: 201 to the browser,\nconfirmation email sent, admin row complete. The only trace was a null\n`meeting_link` column that no view renders. That is why Google Meet could ship\nin v1.1.9, never once produce a link, and go unnoticed until someone asked.\n\nTwo ways out, both cheap:\n\nThe operator now hears about it. A failed generation logs the platform and the\nprovider''s error, and emits a `meeting_link_failed` telemetry event at ERROR.\nThe booking still succeeds either way — the slot is genuinely reserved and a\nlink can be sent by hand — so this stays a report, not a failure path.\n\nThe booker is now told the truth. The email said \"I''ll send you a Google Meet\nlink shortly\", which nothing in the system does: there is no retry, no queue,\nand until this commit no alert. It now says the link could not be generated and\nasks for a reply, which routes the failure to a human through the inbox that\nalready exists.\n\nAlso corrects the OAuth setup script, which told the operator to run\n`wrangler secret put` — the parent repo''s own rule is that the vault broker is\nthe only writer of worker secrets, so a token stored that way is one nothing\nrotates or re-pushes. It now prints the `set-many` call and points at the\nprovisioning doc, and says out loud that the grant must be made as\nmeeting@hadoku.me, since every booking writes an event onto whichever calendar\nauthorizes.","tree":{"sha":"40e8ed8ea7fae2ccaa3c3894c5e3f8bdd07ac4cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/40e8ed8ea7fae2ccaa3c3894c5e3f8bdd07ac4cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09","verification":{"payload":"tree 40e8ed8ea7fae2ccaa3c3894c5e3f8bdd07ac4cd\nparent a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787865371 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787865371 -0700\n\nfix(meetings): report a failed meeting link instead of promising one nothing sends\n\nA booking whose link generation failed was indistinguishable from one that\nworked. The route stored `undefined` and moved on: 201 to the browser,\nconfirmation email sent, admin row complete. The only trace was a null\n`meeting_link` column that no view renders. That is why Google Meet could ship\nin v1.1.9, never once produce a link, and go unnoticed until someone asked.\n\nTwo ways out, both cheap:\n\nThe operator now hears about it. A failed generation logs the platform and the\nprovider''s error, and emits a `meeting_link_failed` telemetry event at ERROR.\nThe booking still succeeds either way — the slot is genuinely reserved and a\nlink can be sent by hand — so this stays a report, not a failure path.\n\nThe booker is now told the truth. The email said \"I''ll send you a Google Meet\nlink shortly\", which nothing in the system does: there is no retry, no queue,\nand until this commit no alert. It now says the link could not be generated and\nasks for a reply, which routes the failure to a human through the inbox that\nalready exists.\n\nAlso corrects the OAuth setup script, which told the operator to run\n`wrangler secret put` — the parent repo''s own rule is that the vault broker is\nthe only writer of worker secrets, so a token stored that way is one nothing\nrotates or re-pushes. It now prints the `set-many` call and points at the\nprovisioning doc, and says out loud that the grant must be made as\nmeeting@hadoku.me, since every booking writes an event onto whichever calendar\nauthorizes.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQL7KSoC1s7dytq6SPcpdfISqRAcUg0XuEc9UxE7eO5tJVgLZS7lM3+3ajnIqw78rox\npqUoBknAe9jtJXPw7zPAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T21:16:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGMyZGRkNTM1MzRkYzRiYTc3MGRhMzk5ZmQ2MDg1ZDI2MTRiOGFmMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8","sha":"a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8"}],"sha":"c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/c2ddd53534dc4ba770da399fd6085d2614b8af09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T20:08:02Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T20:08:02Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(meetings): show the join link, and stop deriving Jitsi rooms from slot ids\n\nThree things stood between a booking and a usable meeting link.\n\nThe browser never saw one. /submit has always returned `meetingLink` in its\n201, and nothing read it — SubmitContactResponse did not even declare the\nfield. The success banner showed date, time and platform, so the booker''s only\nroute to their own meeting was the confirmation email, which is the copy that\ncan be delayed, filtered or bounced. The banner now renders the link when the\nplatform produced one, and renders exactly as before when it did not.\n\nJitsi rooms were guessable. The room was `hadoku-${slotId}`, and slotId is\n`slot-<date>-<ISO start>` — every booked slot id is reconstructible from the\nPUBLIC /appointments/slots listing, which names each slot and says whether it\nis taken. A meet.jit.si room is open to whoever holds its URL, so that made\nevery meeting joinable by a stranger who read the calendar: take the ids marked\nunavailable, prefix `hadoku-`, walk in. Rooms are now 128 bits from the CSPRNG.\nThat also gets the ISO timestamp''s `:` and `.` out of a name the Jitsi UI\nechoes back at participants.\n\nThe Discord invite was a constant in the source. Revoking a leaked invite, or\nmoving servers, meant republishing the package and waiting on a parent deploy.\nIt reads DISCORD_INVITE_URL now, falling back to the compiled-in invite so an\nexisting deployment keeps the invite it already had.\n\nGoogle Meet is unchanged and still returns no link: the code has been complete\nsince v1.1.9 but the OAuth secrets were never provisioned. A booking made\nagainst it still succeeds with meeting_link = null, which is why the banner\ntreats the link as optional rather than gating the success message on it.","tree":{"sha":"600c1f9a80ff3f5cfe84578905c4b49c0d84e917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/600c1f9a80ff3f5cfe84578905c4b49c0d84e917"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8","verification":{"payload":"tree 600c1f9a80ff3f5cfe84578905c4b49c0d84e917\nparent 74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787861282 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787861282 -0700\n\nfix(meetings): show the join link, and stop deriving Jitsi rooms from slot ids\n\nThree things stood between a booking and a usable meeting link.\n\nThe browser never saw one. /submit has always returned `meetingLink` in its\n201, and nothing read it — SubmitContactResponse did not even declare the\nfield. The success banner showed date, time and platform, so the booker''s only\nroute to their own meeting was the confirmation email, which is the copy that\ncan be delayed, filtered or bounced. The banner now renders the link when the\nplatform produced one, and renders exactly as before when it did not.\n\nJitsi rooms were guessable. The room was `hadoku-${slotId}`, and slotId is\n`slot-<date>-<ISO start>` — every booked slot id is reconstructible from the\nPUBLIC /appointments/slots listing, which names each slot and says whether it\nis taken. A meet.jit.si room is open to whoever holds its URL, so that made\nevery meeting joinable by a stranger who read the calendar: take the ids marked\nunavailable, prefix `hadoku-`, walk in. Rooms are now 128 bits from the CSPRNG.\nThat also gets the ISO timestamp''s `:` and `.` out of a name the Jitsi UI\nechoes back at participants.\n\nThe Discord invite was a constant in the source. Revoking a leaked invite, or\nmoving servers, meant republishing the package and waiting on a parent deploy.\nIt reads DISCORD_INVITE_URL now, falling back to the compiled-in invite so an\nexisting deployment keeps the invite it already had.\n\nGoogle Meet is unchanged and still returns no link: the code has been complete\nsince v1.1.9 but the OAuth secrets were never provisioned. A booking made\nagainst it still succeeds with meeting_link = null, which is why the banner\ntreats the link as optional rather than gating the success message on it.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEJyLTMChhVclBVWl3MQOYPWbPpkgu2l6y8yxXcN6HBX39O9TPWS/8Mvh26Q/jFJNl\nhrbseG3CG7Dpx74xmw7wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T21:16:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGE2Yzk3NzVjMzdkOGI0OTdlZjIzYTg4ZTEwODE2MGYzNjVhZjNkZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527","sha":"74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527"}],"sha":"a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/a6c9775c37d8b497ef23a88e108160f365af3de8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T13:05:17Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T13:05:17Z","email":"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: auto-update @wolffm/* to latest","tree":{"sha":"aa1dbbe9ac48dee6935aeb16ae4a4310867abf1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/aa1dbbe9ac48dee6935aeb16ae4a4310867abf1a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDc0YTlkMmMxMDBmZDU4ODFlNzYwM2RhMzAyYzM5MzI2OWY4NjQ1Mjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d","sha":"be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d"}],"sha":"74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/74a9d2c100fd5881e7603da302c393269f864527"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T05:34:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T05:34:05Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): stop the month title flashing white when it has focus\n\nreact-calendar paints #e6e6e6 behind `:enabled:focus`, and the navigation\nbuttons were the one place I left out of the neutraliser — I had swapped\nthem to `:focus-visible` and never covered plain `:focus`. Clicking the\nmonth title focuses it without making it focus-visible, so the library''s\nhardcoded near-white stayed on the button: on a dark card the year picker''s\ntitle read as a solid white bar.\n\nConfirmed it was the library and not a token by reading the focused label\nacross every light theme — rgb(230,230,230) in all of them, regardless of\nwhat `--color-primary-bg` happened to be. My first probe missed it because\nthe pointer was still resting on the label, so `:hover` was winning; the\nbug only shows once hover is out of the picture.\n\nThe nav buttons'' hover and plain focus now sit under the neutraliser, with\nthe tint re-applied below it for hover and `:focus-visible` only. A mouse\nclick leaves no mark, a keyboard tab still gets a visible one, and the\nduplicate copy of the hover rule in the Navigation block is gone — it was\ndead weight, outranked by the neutraliser.","tree":{"sha":"8a24a09094dd709645eae6684d4acdc012971fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/8a24a09094dd709645eae6684d4acdc012971fe5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a24a09094dd709645eae6684d4acdc012971fe5\nparent 60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787722445 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787722445 -0700\n\nfix(ui): stop the month title flashing white when it has focus\n\nreact-calendar paints #e6e6e6 behind `:enabled:focus`, and the navigation\nbuttons were the one place I left out of the neutraliser — I had swapped\nthem to `:focus-visible` and never covered plain `:focus`. Clicking the\nmonth title focuses it without making it focus-visible, so the library''s\nhardcoded near-white stayed on the button: on a dark card the year picker''s\ntitle read as a solid white bar.\n\nConfirmed it was the library and not a token by reading the focused label\nacross every light theme — rgb(230,230,230) in all of them, regardless of\nwhat `--color-primary-bg` happened to be. My first probe missed it because\nthe pointer was still resting on the label, so `:hover` was winning; the\nbug only shows once hover is out of the picture.\n\nThe nav buttons'' hover and plain focus now sit under the neutraliser, with\nthe tint re-applied below it for hover and `:focus-visible` only. A mouse\nclick leaves no mark, a keyboard tab still gets a visible one, and the\nduplicate copy of the hover rule in the Navigation block is gone — it was\ndead weight, outranked by the neutraliser.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCWMBjKT1uhQxbOEBgDiVPqsKB/tA/ghCCaEqokQLPVQxIOAurJ4LqE0CTIGFKyRt7\n6+H858uxisxvCry+8INAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T05:34:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGJlN2NiNGRhY2Y4ZTQ4MGZlMjM2MzAzNWI4YThhZTg0OWFhODgyMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c","sha":"60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c"}],"sha":"be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/be7cb4dacf8e480fe2363035b8a8ae849aa8822d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:41:29Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:41:58Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(ui): stop the time buttons stretching when there are few of them\n\nA grid distributes leftover height INTO its rows — the initial\n`align-content: normal` behaves as `stretch` for auto-sized rows. The\ndesktop rule puts a 6rem floor under the slot grid so it cannot be squeezed\nto nothing when the picker is capped to the window, and with only one row of\ntimes that whole floor went into the row: 96px buttons against their natural\n36px, on exactly the days with the fewest slots to offer.\n\n`align-content: start` keeps the rows their own size and leaves the spare\nroom at the bottom. The buttons are a fixed size; the box around them is\nwhat flexes.\n\nMeasured across all three durations — 32 slots in 5 rows, 16 in 3, 8 in 2,\nplus a forced single row — 36px in every case.","tree":{"sha":"f02b81f4df966b48f25f67e0da1d8ca272e921cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/f02b81f4df966b48f25f67e0da1d8ca272e921cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/60b60f74c2def34c57815cfc938514a93ff6135c","verification":{"payload":"tree f02b81f4df966b48f25f67e0da1d8ca272e921cc\nparent ff82baa772962efe8ac0e98eefb84e6c02e27916\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787697689 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787697718 -0700\n\nfix(ui): stop the time buttons stretching when there are few of them\n\nA grid distributes leftover height INTO its rows — the initial\n`align-content: normal` behaves as `stretch` for auto-sized rows. The\ndesktop rule puts a 6rem floor under the slot grid so it cannot be squeezed\nto nothing when the picker is capped to the window, and with only one row of\ntimes that whole floor went into the row: 96px buttons against their natural\n36px, on exactly the days with the fewest slots to offer.\n\n`align-content: start` keeps the rows their own size and leaves the spare\nroom at the bottom. The buttons are a fixed size; the box around them is\nwhat flexes.\n\nMeasured across all three durations — 32 slots in 5 rows, 16 in 3, 8 in 2,\nplus a forced single row — 36px in every case.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEcqQpyGp11x6pdhP8BEtRjWOqZSo8+DKx8W+tlEbqlcvOTyKWJuuYVC+nepVa6RsA\n1BnOKSox+4Mv7gLNbGQgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T22:42:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type"