hubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3431a71a2a6958f38ef91cb3021ea4aee82cf157/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T04:01:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T04:01:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(deps): declare @wolffm peers as floors, not carets\n\n`pnpm update --latest` in update-wolffm.yml bumps dependencies and\ndevDependencies but never peerDependencies, so a caret peer rots the\nmoment the fleet crosses a major and consumer installs start tripping\npeer conflicts. A floor says what it means: this is the minimum that\nworks, anything newer is fine.\n\nDeclaration only — no version bump and no publish. The real compatibility\ngate is this repo''s CI building against actual latest; the floor just\ndocuments the minimum. Found by hadoku_site''s check:header-fleet\n[stale-peer].","tree":{"sha":"391eea7c81801d375944c8faaec83ece642a21d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/391eea7c81801d375944c8faaec83ece642a21d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/3431a71a2a6958f38ef91cb3021ea4aee82cf157","verification":{"payload":"tree 391eea7c81801d375944c8faaec83ece642a21d9\nparent 63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787025671 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787025671 -0700\n\nchore(deps): declare @wolffm peers as floors, not carets\n\n`pnpm update --latest` in update-wolffm.yml bumps dependencies and\ndevDependencies but never peerDependencies, so a caret peer rots the\nmoment the fleet crosses a major and consumer installs start tripping\npeer conflicts. A floor says what it means: this is the minimum that\nworks, anything newer is fine.\n\nDeclaration only — no version bump and no publish. The real compatibility\ngate is this repo''s CI building against actual latest; the floor just\ndocuments the minimum. Found by hadoku_site''s check:header-fleet\n[stale-peer].\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHr9OVRP+6vEcyJBzA/fwesV9INz0+JH+r2GKFFGtMohYprW94WXb65tvsTCeVTBYt\nizGoMxyOsYoxLVXN117wc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T04:01:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/3431a71a2a6958f38ef91cb3021ea4aee82cf157","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDM0MzFhNzFhMmE2OTU4ZjM4ZWY5MWNiMzAyMWVhNGFlZTgyY2YxNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507","sha":"63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507"}],"sha":"3431a71a2a6958f38ef91cb3021ea4aee82cf157","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/3431a71a2a6958f38ef91cb3021ea4aee82cf157"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T03:21:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T03:21:22Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"chore(deps): pin @wolffm/* ranges to the published versions\n\nFloating ranges (`*`, `>=4.0.0`, `>=1.0.0`, `>=3.0.0`) let the resolver walk\nthis repo across a major with nobody opting in. That is how @wolffm/themes 5.7\ndelivered @wolffm/prefs-client as a REQUIRED peer to every consumer at once:\nnothing in this manifest expressed which version it actually wanted, so there\nwas no range for the change to violate and nothing to fail loudly.\n\n  themes             -> ^5.7.3\n  task-ui-components -> ^4.7.3\n  logger             -> ^1.3.2\n  worker-utils       -> ^1.5.4\n  prefs-client       -> ^1.0.8\n\nPeer ranges move too. On a micro-frontend the peer block is the contract for\nwhat the host''s import map provides, and `*` documents nothing — hadoku_site\nserves themes 5.7.3 / task-ui-components 4.7.3, so that is what the contract\nshould say.\n\nworkspace:* is deliberately untouched: rewriting it to a registry range is\nwhat produced the dual bundled copy behind the 2026-08-05 outage.\n\nVerified: pnpm install clean with no unmet peers, typecheck and build green.","tree":{"sha":"64724838a07ee849d41c1d377858fd6055fe360f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/64724838a07ee849d41c1d377858fd6055fe360f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/63e53a942312180f60fbf153ece969b264b47507","verification":{"payload":"tree 64724838a07ee849d41c1d377858fd6055fe360f\nparent cdc1f51b5476857e168b3daf264c71c6b51bc596\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787023282 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1787023282 -0700\n\nchore(deps): pin @wolffm/* ranges to the published versions\n\nFloating ranges (`*`, `>=4.0.0`, `>=1.0.0`, `>=3.0.0`) let the resolver walk\nthis repo across a major with nobody opting in. That is how @wolffm/themes 5.7\ndelivered @wolffm/prefs-client as a REQUIRED peer to every consumer at once:\nnothing in this manifest expressed which version it actually wanted, so there\nwas no range for the change to violate and nothing to fail loudly.\n\n  themes             -> ^5.7.3\n  task-ui-components -> ^4.7.3\n  logger             -> ^1.3.2\n  worker-utils       -> ^1.5.4\n  prefs-client       -> ^1.0.8\n\nPeer ranges move too. On a micro-frontend the peer block is the contract for\nwhat the host''s import map provides, and `*` documents nothing — hadoku_site\nserves themes 5.7.3 / task-ui-components 4.7.3, so that is what the contract\nshould say.\n\nworkspace:* is deliberately untouched: rewriting it to a registry range is\nwhat produced the dual bundled copy behind the 2026-08-05 outage.\n\nVerified: pnpm install clean with no unmet peers, typecheck and build green.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLlyZjvVa8h3Y4cpAdHvugwCv0+YEPg0ReVb9xh/xMW12Gk+zdceCIXIFLGsAQbFBZ\n9m6e1jFr6r13GnvWH8PQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:21:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url