epos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/c0133e88d5343b92599ab8daab0b4060a8b154ec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/c0133e88d5343b92599ab8daab0b4060a8b154ec","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGMwMTMzZTg4ZDUzNDNiOTI1OTlhYjhkYWFiMGI0MDYwYThiMTU0ZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a","sha":"de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a"}],"sha":"c0133e88d5343b92599ab8daab0b4060a8b154ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/c0133e88d5343b92599ab8daab0b4060a8b154ec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T05:37:45Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T05:37:45Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci(update-wolffm): drop the schedule trigger; the nightly net moved to cron-worker\n\nThe daily safety net is now hadoku_site''s ci:wolffm-fanout, a tail job on the\nrepo-sync Temporal profile (13:00 UTC / 06:00 Pacific) that dispatches\nwolffm_published to every consumer in child-apps.json, and throws on a non-204\nso a dropped dispatch pages Discord.\n\nA Temporal schedule on our own host fires on time. A GitHub Actions schedule\ndoes not: across 46 runs of this same ''0 */6 * * *'' in hadoku-watchparty,\nGitHub fired it a median of +57min late, max +162min, worst at the 00:00 UTC\nslot (median +105min). 00:00 UTC is 17:00 Pacific, and on 2026-08-10 that slot\nlanded at 18:52 Pacific and redeployed production into a live watch party.\n\nFast path unchanged: a publish still dispatches wolffm_published immediately.","tree":{"sha":"de7a829e6475289dc04529032f83c9e689571fe4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/de7a829e6475289dc04529032f83c9e689571fe4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a","verification":{"payload":"tree de7a829e6475289dc04529032f83c9e689571fe4\nparent 0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786426665 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786426665 -0700\n\nci(update-wolffm): drop the schedule trigger; the nightly net moved to cron-worker\n\nThe daily safety net is now hadoku_site''s ci:wolffm-fanout, a tail job on the\nrepo-sync Temporal profile (13:00 UTC / 06:00 Pacific) that dispatches\nwolffm_published to every consumer in child-apps.json, and throws on a non-204\nso a dropped dispatch pages Discord.\n\nA Temporal schedule on our own host fires on time. A GitHub Actions schedule\ndoes not: across 46 runs of this same ''0 */6 * * *'' in hadoku-watchparty,\nGitHub fired it a median of +57min late, max +162min, worst at the 00:00 UTC\nslot (median +105min). 00:00 UTC is 17:00 Pacific, and on 2026-08-10 that slot\nlanded at 18:52 Pacific and redeployed production into a live watch party.\n\nFast path unchanged: a publish still dispatches wolffm_published immediately.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMNhw2LxTSHbn2EYsJDVqqGE3aYCJHREhhprT5jmoYKGAoXy1Y+Gz9LOttg6lIO2G7\nyYQBnVGF/58vHAqzmTuQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T05:53:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGRlMWY1OWFkMThhNjcwYmJlOWFkYmQ2NzliZWMwMjU5NWI2MjE0MmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef","sha":"0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef"}],"sha":"de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/de1f59ad18a670bbe9adbd679bec02595b62142a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T03:10:11Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T03:10:23Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"feat(email): outbound display name is \"Matthaeus Wolff\", and configurable\n\nMail sent from matthaeus@hadoku.me arrived showing \"Hadoku Mail\" — a brand\nwhere a person belongs. The display name is the most prominent thing in a\nrecipient''s inbox list and often the only thing read before deciding to open,\nso a reply from a human announcing itself as a system reads like a ticketing\nrobot. That is the opposite of what this domain''s outbound mail is for:\nrecruiters and business contacts replying to a person.\n\nSame mistake as the /resume link-preview card that said \"Hadoku - Resume\".\n\nThe string was hardcoded SEPARATELY in both providers (resend.ts and\nmailchannels.ts) with no configuration point anywhere, so changing it meant\nediting two files that could silently disagree about who the sender is. Now:\n\n- EMAIL_CONFIG.DEFAULT_FROM_NAME is the single source, next to DEFAULT_FROM\n- EmailParams.fromName overrides per message\n- the EMAIL_FROM_NAME binding overrides per deployment, so the name can change\n  from wrangler.toml without a package release\n\nPinned with tests, because this is precisely the class of string that\nregresses silently — nothing fails to compile, no test breaks, and nobody\nnotices until it is in front of the person you were trying to impress. The\nsuite asserts the default, asserts it does NOT contain \"hadoku\", and checks\nboth providers honour both the default and an override.","tree":{"sha":"734f899a6dc44ca24bbfb9047d75719e1d4d762a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/734f899a6dc44ca24bbfb9047d75719e1d4d762a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef","verification":{"payload":"tree 734f899a6dc44ca24bbfb9047d75719e1d4d762a\nparent aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786245011 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786245023 -0700\n\nfeat(email): outbound display name is \"Matthaeus Wolff\", and configurable\n\nMail sent from matthaeus@hadoku.me arrived showing \"Hadoku Mail\" — a brand\nwhere a person belongs. The display name is the most prominent thing in a\nrecipient''s inbox list and often the only thing read before deciding to open,\nso a reply from a human announcing itself as a system reads like a ticketing\nrobot. That is the opposite of what this domain''s outbound mail is for:\nrecruiters and business contacts replying to a person.\n\nSame mistake as the /resume link-preview card that said \"Hadoku - Resume\".\n\nThe string was hardcoded SEPARATELY in both providers (resend.ts and\nmailchannels.ts) with no configuration point anywhere, so changing it meant\nediting two files that could silently disagree about who the sender is. Now:\n\n- EMAIL_CONFIG.DEFAULT_FROM_NAME is the single source, next to DEFAULT_FROM\n- EmailParams.fromName overrides per message\n- the EMAIL_FROM_NAME binding overrides per deployment, so the name can change\n  from wrangler.toml without a package release\n\nPinned with tests, because this is precisely the class of string that\nregresses silently — nothing fails to compile, no test breaks, and nobody\nnotices until it is in front of the person you were trying to impress. The\nsuite asserts the default, asserts it does NOT contain \"hadoku\", and checks\nboth providers honour both the default and an override.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLBMqdvUXKojKVGUH7jCle+CmFebXtpESYdb5bI1f6YWn0tfTO9mJaB3MJkfKoGyS3\nwM+7ppkEHN1TJiOhn0qwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-09T13:29:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKDAzNjJkNDU5NDZkZTI3YzlhYTk0YzBlNGQwYzE2ZGI2ODU2OTE1ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494","sha":"aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494"}],"sha":"0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/0362d45946de27c9aa94c0e4d0c16db6856915ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:12:13Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:14:15Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"ci: make the runner pool steerable for hosted fallback\n\nruns-on now reads vars.CI_RUNNER with the claw pool as the literal\ndefault, so behaviour is unchanged while the variable is unset. During\na full claw outage mgmt-api''s runner-health sets it to ubuntu-latest and\nclears it when a claw returns.\n\nDriven by runner availability, never by job outcome — a red build is\nnever retried or rehomed.","tree":{"sha":"d503d6fe87dbc3bbf9f57b6675d9c3a7a6b324e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/d503d6fe87dbc3bbf9f57b6675d9c3a7a6b324e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494","verification":{"payload":"tree d503d6fe87dbc3bbf9f57b6675d9c3a7a6b324e2\nparent 8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786234333 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786234455 -0700\n\nci: make the runner pool steerable for hosted fallback\n\nruns-on now reads vars.CI_RUNNER with the claw pool as the literal\ndefault, so behaviour is unchanged while the variable is unset. During\na full claw outage mgmt-api''s runner-health sets it to ubuntu-latest and\nclears it when a claw returns.\n\nDriven by runner availability, never by job outcome — a red build is\nnever retried or rehomed.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKd5kLwLhkUKuRtx7Jsxw03NTkz0s3lfAQQttTE8i4RAgh2kqLKEUzk7zjI7DRnIus\nSrgqYpJO18lcIJ1Yderg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-09T00:19:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494","node_id":"C_kwDOQZHnxNoAKGFhZjQwMGRhMmY4MjI2YTgwMzIwMGRlODg2MTA2OGI5MDdjZGU0OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commit/8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5","sha":"8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5"}],"sha":"aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/aaf400da2f8226a803200de8861068b907cde494"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/WolffM","id":8714327,"login":"WolffM","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3MTQzMjc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/commits/8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T22:35:55Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T22:35:55Z","email":"8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com","name":"WolffM"},"message":"fix(api): typecheck the api/ tree, and fix the 18 errors it was hiding\n\n`pnpm run typecheck` was `tsc --noEmit`, which uses the root tsconfig — and\nthat includes only `src/**/*`. tsconfig.api.json existed but no script, hook or\nCI job ever ran it, and `build:api` is tsup, which strips types without\nchecking them. So the entire api/ tree — the worker that actually runs — has\nnever been typechecked, and had accumulated 18 errors.\n\ntypecheck now runs both configs, so CI and the pre-commit hook cover api/ with\nno workflow change.\n\nEvery fix addresses the cause rather than silencing the symptom:\n\n- resend.ts — `Response.json()` is `unknown`, correctly. Declared the two\n  response shapes instead of casting. Both fields stay optional: the error path\n  already falls back, and asserting them would move a handled fallback into a\n  runtime undefined. Dropping `data.id as string` is safe — `messageId` is\n  already `string | undefined` on EmailResponse.\n\n- storage/{submissions,appointments}.ts — `globalThis.crypto` does not\n  typecheck: workers-types declares `crypto` via `declare const`, which\n  TypeScript does not expose as a globalThis property. The `as { randomUUID }`\n  cast was there because of that and is exactly what hid it. Now plain\n  `crypto.randomUUID()`, with the global declared in eslint.config.js so\n  no-undef accepts it.\n\n- database.ts — page_count/page_size arrive from a D1 PRAGMA as `unknown`.\n  Number() rather than `as number`: the cast would have compiled while\n  yielding NaN for a non-numeric value, which is the silent-garbage outcome a\n  capacity warning must not have.\n\n- types.ts + meeting-links.ts — JITSI_DOMAIN and the GOOGLE_OAUTH_* bindings\n  were READ but never declared on ContactEnv, which is why generateMeetingLink\n  took `Record<string, unknown>`. Declaring them lets that parameter be\n  ContactEnv and removes two casts, including\n  `env as Parameters<typeof createGoogleMeetEvent>[1]`. A typo in a binding\n  name is now a compile error.\n\n- validation.ts — validateSlotFetchRequest took `string | null` while its only\n  caller passes `c.req.query()`, which is `string | undefined`. The narrow type\n  never made the absent case impossible; it just made the real call site fail.\n\n- storage/{submissions,templates}.ts — PAGINATION_DEFAULTS is `as const`, so\n  `limit = PAGINATION_DEFAULTS.LIMIT` infers the LITERAL `100`, and passing any\n  number fails. Annotated `: number`, matching what appointments.ts already\n  did. Note the destructured defaults in templates.ts listEmailTemplates must\n  NOT be annotated — `limit: number` there renames the binding rather than\n  typing it, and its interface already declares the type.\n\n- routes/admin/index.ts — ContentfulStatusCode is not exported from the hono\n  root; it lives in hono/utils/http-status.\n\n- inbound-forwarders.ts — the ContactEnv → Record cast now goes via `unknown`.\n  This one IS a genuine dynamic read (urlEnv/keyEnv are runtime strings), so\n  the escape hatch stays, narrowed to the one place it is needed.\n\n- tsconfig.api.json pinned `@cloudflare/workers-types/2023-07-01` while\n  wrangler runs compatibility_date 2025-01-11. Switched to the current\n  entrypoint. It changed none of the 18 errors, but types three years behind\n  the runtime they describe are their own latent bug.\n\n170 tests still pass; lint, format, build and both typechecks green.","tree":{"sha":"b38f38e048fb7161e72323970152ab6952c6d309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/trees/b38f38e048fb7161e72323970152ab6952c6d309"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WolffM/hadoku-contact-ui/git/commits/8a7a8a4c6bdeaa696a240bc372360018966488a5","verification":{"payload":"tree b38f38e048fb7161e72323970152ab6952c6d309\nparent 5fde0d1b2be865d2618b60ac10be4acb81c43c38\nauthor WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786228555 -0700\ncommitter WolffM <8714327+WolffM@users.noreply.github.com> 1786228555 -0700\n\nfix(api): typecheck the api/ tree, and fix the 18 errors it was hiding\n\n`pnpm run typecheck` was `tsc --noEmit`, which uses the root tsconfig — and\nthat includes only `src/**/*`. tsconfig.api.json existed but no script, hook or\nCI job ever ran it, and `build:api` is tsup, which strips types without\nchecking them. So the entire api/ tree — the worker that actually runs — has\nnever been typechecked, and had accumulated 18 errors.\n\ntypecheck now runs both configs, so CI and the pre-commit hook cover api/ with\nno workflow change.\n\nEvery fix addresses the cause rather than silencing the symptom:\n\n- resend.ts — `Response.json()` is `unknown`, correctly. Declared the two\n  response shapes instead of casting. Both fields stay optional: the error path\n  already falls back, and asserting them would move a handled fallback into a\n  runtime undefined. Dropping `data.id as string` is safe — `messageId` is\n  already `string | undefined` on EmailResponse.\n\n- storage/{submissions,appointments}.ts — `globalThis.crypto` does not\n  typecheck: workers-types declares `crypto` via `declare const`, which\n  TypeScript does not expose as a globalThis property. The `as { randomUUID }`\n  cast was there because of that and is exactly what hid it. Now plain\n  `crypto.randomUUID()`, with the global declared in eslint.config.js so\n  no-undef accepts it.\n\n- database.ts — page_count/page_size arrive from a D1 PRAGMA as `unknown`.\n  Number() rather than `as number`: the cast would have compiled while\n  yielding NaN for a non-numeric value, which is the silent-garbage outcome a\n  capacity warning must not have.\n\n- types.ts + meeting-links.ts — JITSI_DOMAIN and the GOOGLE_OAUTH_* bindings\n  were READ but never declared on ContactEnv, which is why generateMeetingLink\n  took `Record<string, unknown>`. Declaring them lets that parameter be\n  ContactEnv and removes two casts, including\n  `env as Parameters<typeof createGoogleMeetEvent>[1]`. A typo in a binding\n  name is now a compile error.\n\n- validation.ts — validateSlotFetchRequest took `string | null` while its only\n  caller passes `c.req.query()`, which is `string | undefined`. The narrow type\n  never made the absent case impossible; it just made the real call site fail.\n\n- storage/{submissions,templates}.ts — PAGINATION_DEFAULTS is `as const`, so\n  `limit = PAGINATION_DEFAULTS.LIMIT` infers the LITERAL `100`, and passing any\n  number fails. Annotated `: number`, matching what appointments.ts already\n  did. Note the destructured defaults in templates.ts listEmailTemplates must\n  NOT be annotated — `limit: number` there renames the binding rather than\n  typing it, and its interface already declares the type.\n\n- routes/admin/index.ts — ContentfulStatusCode is not exported from the hono\n  root; it lives in hono/utils/http-status.\n\n- inbound-forwarders.ts — the ContactEnv → Record cast now goes via `unknown`.\n  This one IS a genuine dynamic read (urlEnv/keyEnv are runtime strings), so\n  the escape hatch stays, narrowed to the one place it is needed.\n\n- tsconfig.api.json pinned `@cloudflare/workers-types/2023-07-01` while\n  wrangler runs compatibility_date 2025-01-11. Switched to the current\n  entrypoint. It changed none of the 18 errors, but types three years behind\n  the runtime they describe are their own latent bug.\n\n170 tests still pass; lint, format, build and both typechecks green.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgtExEZCroNtll/b5fn53fujqeNd\nwjYFlHwlmteH8Ve7QAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPF8X8dkueesNnryx+C937l/5xPLWU9c4UV66YYp1rShDPkJXp8phT6XXX14BtMyvl\n8z1xQEx0bW3xIS4nQ6Kg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-09T00:19:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8714327?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WolffM/followers","following_url":"ht