ogin":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smonier/js-store-locator/commit/7f157bed05787fb373a76326d04736373bbbaee9","node_id":"C_kwDOQZvg0NoAKDdmMTU3YmVkMDU3ODdmYjM3M2E3NjMyNmQwNDczNjM3M2JiYmFlZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smonier/js-store-locator/commit/9ab35b89f63d9237eb8155bf2600e2d3f4308f96","sha":"9ab35b89f63d9237eb8155bf2600e2d3f4308f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smonier/js-store-locator/commits/9ab35b89f63d9237eb8155bf2600e2d3f4308f96"}],"sha":"7f157bed05787fb373a76326d04736373bbbaee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smonier/js-store-locator/commits/7f157bed05787fb373a76326d04736373bbbaee9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smonier/js-store-locator/commits/9ab35b89f63d9237eb8155bf2600e2d3f4308f96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:10:59Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T10:10:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: accessible store locator (RGAA 4.1.2), sturdier store data rendering (#1)\n\n* build: build the views and the island again next to the UI extension\n\nThe Vite configuration only built the jContent UI extension, so a fresh\nbuild shipped no server views and no client island. The default mode now\nbuilds the template-set code into dist/ and the ui mode builds the UI\nextension into javascript/apps.\n\n* fix: serve the map stylesheet from the module\n\nThe island already bundles the Leaflet stylesheet into the module''s\nstyle.css, so the views no longer add a second copy from a third-party\nhost.\n\n* feat: make the store locator and the store page accessible (RGAA 4.1.2)\n\nStore locator:\n- the island is rendered on the server: without JavaScript the visitor\n  gets the full store list, each name linking to the store''s own page;\n  the map, the selection and the open/closed status start in the browser\n- no h1 in the component: the heading starts one level below a titled\n  container (h3 in a free zone, h2 elsewhere), store names one level below\n- the search field has a visible label, and the number of results is a\n  role=\"status\" message (RGAA 7.5)\n- the list is a list; each store name is a button with aria-pressed, the\n  details panel takes the focus, and Escape or the named close button\n  gives it back to the list\n- the map is a named region described as equivalent to the list; markers\n  are keyboard buttons named after the store (Enter and Space), zoom\n  controls and attribution are translated, tiles use the current\n  OpenStreetMap URL; stores without coordinates stay in the list only\n- open/closed is text with a symbol, never colour alone; it is computed\n  from the visitor''s clock after hydration and hidden for stores without\n  opening hours (they were all shown as closed)\n- opening hours are a table covering the whole week (closed days\n  included, consecutive days grouped), times formatted for the locale\n- the two panes stack below 48rem (reflow at 320 px), no fixed heights\n  clip text with increased spacing, focus ring 3 px at 3:1 or more,\n  targets 44 px, motion off under prefers-reduced-motion\n- colours, radius and shadow read --jsstoreloc-* custom properties with\n  the current values as fallbacks; the panel sets its own text colour and\n  colour scheme, so it stays readable on a dark page\n- external links no longer open a new window; link texts that repeat\n  carry the store name for screen readers\n- store data is read once on the server into plain values, with links\n  normalised there, and the views render those values as they are; the\n  view adds the folder and the stores as cache dependencies\n\nStore page: new fullPage and default views (the main-resource page was\nempty), with the store name as h1 and the same details as the panel.\n\nAll new strings are in English and French.\n\n* fix(i18n): translate the content-manager previews\n\nThe previews of the app and of a store had English labels written in the\nviews. They now read the module''s EN and FR locale files, list the stores\nof the picked folder, and render the store links from the checked store\nvalues.\n\n* chore: make yarn lint pass\n\nSkip the files generated by the federation build and drop an unused\ncatch binding.\n\n* fix: map controls follow the panel colours on dark hosts\n\n* fix(store): phone and website links, amenities, headings and ids of the store views\n\n- tel: links carry the number itself: an extension (ext., x, poste, #,\n  ;ext=) stays in the visible text only, and a \"(0)\" written after the\n  country code is not dialled.\n- Website addresses starting with \"www.\" are read as https, and paths\n  with an apostrophe are kept; only http and https are linked.\n- Each amenity is listed once.\n- The fullPage view is kept out of the view picker, and both store views\n  render the name as h1 only when the store is the main resource;\n  elsewhere the name steps down under a titled container.\n- Element ids are unique per rendering, so a store shown twice on a page\n  keeps distinct ids.\n- The locator and the store views declare the store images as cache\n  dependencies.\n\n* fix(hours): one reading of all-day slots for the table and the status\n\n- A slot from 00:00 to 23:59, or one that opens and closes at the same\n  time, is listed as open 24 hours and counts as open all that day.\n- A closing time of 23:59 includes that last minute.\n- French day ranges read \"Du lundi au vendredi\".\n\n* fix(locator): focus, map framing, map credits and search\n\n- Closing the details gives the focus back to the control that opened\n  them (marker or list button), or to another visible control for the\n  same store, the search field or the list toggle.\n- Selecting a store, including the one already shown, centres the map on\n  it and focuses its details; side by side, the marker is centred in the\n  part of the map above the details panel.\n- The map credits are a line below the map, outside the panel.\n- The selected store button carries aria-current.\n- The search ignores accents (\"orleans\" finds \"Orléans\"), and a store\n  left out by the search closes its details.\n- A store view paints the themed surface under the themed text.\n\n* test: unit tests for the opening hours, search and link helpers, run in CI\n\n- Vitest, table-driven: parseOpeningHours, isAllDay, isOpenAt (overnight,\n  midnight and all-day slots), groupOpeningHours (EN and FR), the\n  accent-insensitive search, telephoneHref, safeWebUrl and uniqueValues.\n- `yarn test` runs them; the CI build job uses Node 22, installs with an\n  immutable lockfile, then runs lint, tests and the build.\n\n* build: yarn dev builds the UI extension, then watches the views\n\n- `yarn dev` (and `yarn watch`) builds the jContent UI extension once,\n  so the packed module carries the opening-hours editor, then watches\n  the views and the island.\n- README: search, opening-hours conventions, focus behaviour, the test\n  script, and the time zone the open/closed status reads.","tree":{"sha":"f4fc4c1bb55dd271254a6e418646411917785f06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smonier/js-store-locator/git/trees/f4fc4c1bb55dd271254a6e418646411917785f06"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smonier/js-store-locator/git/commits/9ab35b89f63d9237eb8155bf2600e2d3f4308f96","verification":{"payload":"tree f4fc4c1bb55dd271254a6e418646411917785f06\nparent 7c6c3dec450cc62f0572646427deb1c23dc205b9\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1790849459 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790849459 +0200\n\nfeat: accessible store locator (RGAA 4.1.2), sturdier store data rendering (#1)\n\n* build: build the views and the island again next to the UI extension\n\nThe Vite configuration only built the jContent UI extension, so a fresh\nbuild shipped no server views and no client island. The default mode now\nbuilds the template-set code into dist/ and the ui mode builds the UI\nextension into javascript/apps.\n\n* fix: serve the map stylesheet from the module\n\nThe island already bundles the Leaflet stylesheet into the module''s\nstyle.css, so the views no longer add a second copy from a third-party\nhost.\n\n* feat: make the store locator and the store page accessible (RGAA 4.1.2)\n\nStore locator:\n- the island is rendered on the server: without JavaScript the visitor\n  gets the full store list, each name linking to the store''s own page;\n  the map, the selection and the open/closed status start in the browser\n- no h1 in the component: the heading starts one level below a titled\n  container (h3 in a free zone, h2 elsewhere), store names one level below\n- the search field has a visible label, and the number of results is a\n  role=\"status\" message (RGAA 7.5)\n- the list is a list; each store name is a button with aria-pressed, the\n  details panel takes the focus, and Escape or the named close button\n  gives it back to the list\n- the map is a named region described as equivalent to the list; markers\n  are keyboard buttons named after the store (Enter and Space), zoom\n  controls and attribution are translated, tiles use the current\n  OpenStreetMap URL; stores without coordinates stay in the list only\n- open/closed is text with a symbol, never colour alone; it is computed\n  from the visitor''s clock after hydration and hidden for stores without\n  opening hours (they were all shown as closed)\n- opening hours are a table covering the whole week (closed days\n  included, consecutive days grouped), times formatted for the locale\n- the two panes stack below 48rem (reflow at 320 px), no fixed heights\n  clip text with increased spacing, focus ring 3 px at 3:1 or more,\n  targets 44 px, motion off under prefers-reduced-motion\n- colours, radius and shadow read --jsstoreloc-* custom properties with\n  the current values as fallbacks; the panel sets its own text colour and\n  colour scheme, so it stays readable on a dark page\n- external links no longer open a new window; link texts that repeat\n  carry the store name for screen readers\n- store data is read once on the server into plain values, with links\n  normalised there, and the views render those values as they are; the\n  view adds the folder and the stores as cache dependencies\n\nStore page: new fullPage and default views (the main-resource page was\nempty), with the store name as h1 and the same details as the panel.\n\nAll new strings are in English and French.\n\n* fix(i18n): translate the content-manager previews\n\nThe previews of the app and of a store had English labels written in the\nviews. They now read the module''s EN and FR locale files, list the stores\nof the picked folder, and render the store links from the checked store\nvalues.\n\n* chore: make yarn lint pass\n\nSkip the files generated by the federation build and drop an unused\ncatch binding.\n\n* fix: map controls follow the panel colours on dark hosts\n\n* fix(store): phone and website links, amenities, headings and ids of the store views\n\n- tel: links carry the number itself: an extension (ext., x, poste, #,\n  ;ext=) stays in the visible text only, and a \"(0)\" written after the\n  country code is not dialled.\n- Website addresses starting with \"www.\" are read as https, and paths\n  with an apostrophe are kept; only http and https are linked.\n- Each amenity is listed once.\n- The fullPage view is kept out of the view picker, and both store views\n  render the name as h1 only when the store is the main resource;\n  elsewhere the name steps down under a titled container.\n- Element ids are unique per rendering, so a store shown twice on a page\n  keeps distinct ids.\n- The locator and the store views declare the store images as cache\n  dependencies.\n\n* fix(hours): one reading of all-day slots for the table and the status\n\n- A slot from 00:00 to 23:59, or one that opens and closes at the same\n  time, is listed as open 24 hours and counts as open all that day.\n- A closing time of 23:59 includes that last minute.\n- French day ranges read \"Du lundi au vendredi\".\n\n* fix(locator): focus, map framing, map credits and search\n\n- Closing the details gives the focus back to the control that opened\n  them (marker or list button), or to another visible control for the\n  same store, the search field or the list toggle.\n- Selecting a store, including the one already shown, centres the map on\n  it and focuses its details; side by side, the marker is centred in the\n  part of the map above the details panel.\n- The map credits are a line below the map, outside the panel.\n- The selected store button carries aria-current.\n- The search ignores accents (\"orleans\" finds \"Orléans\"), and a store\n  left out by the search closes its details.\n- A store view paints the themed surface under the themed text.\n\n* test: unit tests for the opening hours, search and link helpers, run in CI\n\n- Vitest, table-driven: parseOpeningHours, isAllDay, isOpenAt (overnight,\n  midnight and all-day slots), groupOpeningHours (EN and FR), the\n  accent-insensitive search, telephoneHref, safeWebUrl and uniqueValues.\n- `yarn test` runs them; the CI build job uses Node 22, installs with an\n  immutable lockfile, then runs lint, tests and the build.\n\n* build: yarn dev builds the UI extension, then watches the views\n\n- `yarn dev` (and `yarn watch`) builds the jContent UI extension once,\n  so the packed module carries the opening-hours editor, then watches\n  the views and the island.\n- README: search, opening-hours conventions, focus behaviour, the test\n  script, and the time zone the open/closed status reads.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvjG0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVFoQAGotW8KNCtNahtdMtp26aCBr\n696JHrRDuM2KO9I00NgACw8BsMUT6CAswQioxMhy2qlPdrfClFqYcs745c6dFzwt\nG94C0fTN+N7HNIkIc60pqcyrhef8K4ecaAD8fwmWv3BscwMpxzZn3hRxPqzepgoX\nECSq+XQRLiYZNrkVFLiRLYv6qkOAsufk2qmlUktdlHlnAstmZeQBj3MDCzw+e1W0\n93QPKsub3xXuaz8CZhoRAcbI9BtM4rNjS3WslppelKySdvWchS4hmX4X5M4q3CA1\nXeZZ/Szn4IAqtxxPxuGiTR2abh9ucqE3CLiFcvnoMW8gGQK9s9FL/E7tQol8KbB2\ncz6cPU7aDASx6+BkP1Y/IO2uZ22WoIVjkPoc/s/hISQ4E46bihYytejBG3BkyHC+\n9xrGGMYgbT7bHp6FAlc6RJQrtlIkVeLbCl0DUcxDPaYhEn+FGOI8920swQ63HRSA\nXXeTTltQFpqSy4cAManuN0HdGd0Z7qta59u+bk/gux51Coys57k4XB+5Xw9ihhF8\nSykHFriPBN8cz8Eo8Ga8XbZSl0JFJgIqg8abRFJgBXycsoEh1G6oX1ifhOT/LyHn\nlZ4phms6lkFfjXcl19BcLInIgRuK8LYbI+V+OF6K6fCX7QvslytjMdIb/O7Fwvg+\nURKblmzpUhvuJf/rT1qf\n=BrC1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T10:11:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.